{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note","id":14870,"title":"Scion 2: A Developer's Note","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-20T13:50:45-08:00","id":14870,"title":"Scion 2: A Developer's Note","content":"Hello, all. I'm throwing down a little introduction and update for folks here. It'll be similar to the one I had on the old forums, most likely. I'm a pretty predictable guy.<br /> <br /> My name is Joseph Carriker, and I'm the developer-type for the new Scion line. I'm an avid mythology nerd and amateur folklorist, a practicing polytheist and did some writing on the old Scion (in particular, in Scion: Demigod, I designed the Touchstones and the myriad Underworlds there). I've written for a bunch of New World of Darkness (including having been developer for Vampire: the Requiem for a while), a bunch of Exalted Second Edition, and do plenty of other freelancing in addition to all that.<br /> <br /> At current, we're putting the finishing touches on a baseline system for the new Scion. Rather than simply pick up the old system, we decided to build one from the ground up, to better suit our needs for issues of things like scaling and player-driven narratives. That can be a pretty exhaustive process, even when the developer *doesn't* have to deal with recent spinal surgeries. I did, though, back at the beginning of October, so you've all got my deepest apologies: I'm the reason things are running a little behind where we'd like them. That's also the reason I've been a presence here in name spoken by others only.<br /> <br /> At this point, though, we're about to enter a &quot;hammering on the systems&quot; phase of the design, and to get folks writing on both systems and non-systems portions of both Scion: Origins and Scion: Hero, so that's all about to pick up like crazy. I'm not a big community development type, I'll admit. I admire my fellow developers who can lay out everything they're working on as they're working on it. I'm just a bit more of a hermit when it comes to my creative process, I fear.<br /> <br /> That said, do keep an eye out for more of these developer's notes. I'm going to use them as a means of communicating some of the new or improved elements of our game, and get some conversation going about them. I'm also here to answer any questions you might have, but I'll be super up-front with you right now: I probably don't have the answers to anything but the most general of questions at this time.<br /> <br /> I will say this, though: &quot;Hero&quot; is going to include ten full pantheons, and my goal is to have a handful more each in both &quot;Demigod&quot; and &quot;God&quot;. That may fall by the wayside, depending on the needs of the books themselves, but I like a world full of possibilities, and I think that's a great way to start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Regards,<br /> Joseph D. Carriker<br /> -------------------------------------------<br /> \u201cIn Springtime, O Dionysos, To thy holy temple come,<br /> To Elis with thy Graces, Rushing with thy bull-foot, come,<br /> Noble Bull, Noble Bull\u201d<br /> \u2015 Plutarch","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1242-jdcarriker","name":"JDCarriker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T14:26:59-08:00","id":14882,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the news Oakthorne, I hope you feel better!<br /> <br /> I love the news that we are getting 10 Pantheons to start with and more with each of the books! Please take all the time you need developing the game! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T15:09:38-08:00","id":14896,"title":"","content":"Can you share any thoughts you have on Fate and Fatebinding?<br /> <br /> It was the biggest part of Scion 1 that I found tough to use but seemed like it should be really important to the setting.<br /> <br /> I don't care about mechanics (especially if you're still hammering them!) but have you given it any thought? Listed some ideas and discarded them all? Followed one thought thread and abandoned it at the last moment? etc.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T16:03:57-08:00","id":14928,"title":"","content":"If you don't mind my asking; What gods do you worship? Are you an asatru or are you more Greek or something else? I'm just curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T16:08:19-08:00","id":14933,"title":"","content":"I approve of this thread and others like. I don't have much else to say at this point, I'm afraid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T16:15:20-08:00","id":14937,"title":"","content":"Hi there, hopefully you're having a good recovery.<br /> <br /> I would like to say that really like the concept of Touchstones, it is useful from a myth making and game stand point and isn't what everyone immediately imagines when playing Gods, my players were expecting to go to the Underworld and to the Overworld, but got really happy to find the Touchstones and after a while using them to travel.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, can you tell us anything about the general guide lines that are defining Scion 2? Like what is the relevance of Fate (narrative tool vs. mechanic tool)? How do you intend to convey the feeling of playing a God (are Epics and their crazy success scale still a thing)? Any change to the Metaphysics of the game (concerning places like Underworlds, Godrealms, Titanrealms, the influence of the Parent God and Pantheon....)? Are we going to be able to take what was given for Scion 1 and transfer it to Scion 2 (assuming that players will reach Demigod and God stages before the actual books cover it)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T18:03:46-08:00","id":15016,"title":"","content":"Glad to see that you are up and writing on the boards. Looking forward to hearing more. I think I'm mostly keen on the crunchy bits of the mechanics. I think I'm glad to see a new ground up system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T19:00:34-08:00","id":15044,"title":"","content":"Ten pantheons sounds like a really solid start for the game. That's a lot of potential for a group.<br /> <br /> More pantheons is obviously better, but are Demigod and God the right place to stick them? Maybe just have an additional pantheons pdf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T19:49:57-08:00","id":15065,"title":"","content":"Speedy recovery and well wishes! Ten pantheons makes me giddy and curious all at once. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">At the end of the day, what works in <b>YOUR</b> story with <b>YOUR</b> players is what matters most. Not what someone on some forum says.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/328-phoenixfire","name":"PhoenixFire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar328_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T19:49:59-08:00","id":15066,"title":"","content":"1) Part of the original concern for the original game seemed to be &quot;Scion or bust&quot;. Basically it felt as if Scion's where the only people who really often mattered in the world. Aside from the Scions, are there going to more emphasis put out for other supernatural forces within the world? Neall(?) already did a good job of discussing some things, so I'm curious to how else the world is going to be fleshed out.<br /> <br /> 2) Any information about how new boons work would be amazing. Will there be more aside from the 1-3 level? I know you could make custom boons, but I do feel like having a few options for each level listed in the official book really helps out people who suck at making their own powers.<br /> <br /> 3) Please tell me that Sci will be coming back! Please!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T00:31:33-08:00","id":15200,"title":"","content":"Is the system still recognizable as the Storyteller system?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is a signature &lt;-----------","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/118-shining-dragon","name":"Shining Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T07:20:50-08:00","id":15354,"title":"","content":"Good to hear from you, Mr. Carriker. I very much hope you're recovering quickly from your surgeries and hope you'll be firing on all cylinders very soon.<br /> <br /> Thank you so much for coming here to give us this update. I love how the devs of all these games are so open and approachable with the fans.<br /> <br /> Scion is one of my very favorite games, and I'm delighted to hear that this time it's getting what it should have had all along: a custom-designed system as well as having the devs approach it more like an ongoing series rather than just three books. I see no reason at all why Scion can't be just as big a game as Exalted, and I'm thrilled that it sounds like that's how you're approaching it.<br /> <br /> Awesome news about the ten pantheons to start with! I know my players will be happy to have four more choices right from the jump. It sounds to me like you're exactly the right team to bring Scion to the level of glory it truly deserves.<br /> <br /> Thanks again for speaking to us. Look forward to hearing more soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T07:45:26-08:00","id":15368,"title":"","content":"Pleased to meet you Dev. Carriker, I wish you a speedy recovery!<br /> <br /> The idea of 10 core pantheons has me excstatic. I presume that these 10 core will be composed of the previous official pantheons? (i.e. Greek, Norse, African, Aztec, Egyptian, Japanese + Chinese, Persian, Irish, &amp; Hindu?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T07:58:39-08:00","id":15380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shining Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=15200#post15200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the system still recognizable as the Storyteller system?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends what you mean. The system <b>isn't</b> Storyteller (any of the many, many versions of it), or Storytelling (either version). The rules team includes people who've worked on Trinity 1st, cWoD Storyteller Revised, the *20 version of Storyteller from V20, W20, and M20, Storytelling, GMC Storytelling from God-Machine, Demon, Strix, Idigam, and Fallen World... You can recognise elements drawn from all of them, and elements that are completely new.<br /> <br /> It uses d10s, and the character sheet has dots on it.<br /> <br /> <br /> For reference:<br /> <br /> Storyteller - the original engine, used from Vampire: The Masquerade to Wraith: The Great War, with slight variations like Werewolf's original combat system along the way.<br /> <br /> Storyteller (Trinity) - the fixed-target number, skills linked to attributes version used in the Trinity, Aberrent, and Adventure 1st editions.<br /> <br /> Storyteller Revised - Vampire: The Masquerade Revised through to Orpheus, which imported some design from Trinity.<br /> <br /> Storyteller (Exalted) - the 1st edition of Exalted, technically based on Trinity's system, not the cWoD's. Includes a 1.5 version in the players guide that changes the combat rules.<br /> <br /> Storyteller (Ex2) - the system Exalted 2nd and Scion use, with tick-based combat.<br /> <br /> Storyteller (Ex3) - the system for Exalted's new edition.<br /> <br /> Storytelling - the nWoD system, different from any of the above. Fixed(ish) TNs, one success is a success, Power/Finesse/Resistance stats.<br /> <br /> Storytelling (GMC) - the updated nWoD system from Demon onwards, and the Chronicle Books.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So... Which Storyteller do you mean?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T11:06:29-08:00","id":15482,"title":"","content":"I think the question is more if it will stay in the Storyteller/ing lineage of systems, rather than if it will be the direct &quot;child&quot; of one of the existing ones. So beyond things like d10s and dots, the baseline human 0-5 scale, having Attributes and Abilities/Skills added together for dice-pools, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T12:26:16-08:00","id":15523,"title":"","content":"It will have elements recognizable to Storyteller/ing players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T12:58:47-08:00","id":15551,"title":"","content":"that was carefully worded <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T13:32:39-08:00","id":15584,"title":"","content":"Indeed. I appreciate that Scion and Trinity are now Onyx Path properties and there's no requirement to keep them tied to the ST lineage of systems. I'm not sure how I'd personally, or the fans in general, are going to react if they get taken too far away from their system roots though. What makes something a ST lineage system is pretty vague as it stands, so there's plenty of room for a lot of variation, before people are going to say, &quot;this just isn't a ST game!&quot; I personally doubt that Scion 2e is going to get that far removed from its predecessor. I also appreciate that the system isn't done yet, so even the teams working on it don't know exactly how close it will look in the end.<br /> <br /> At the same time, I'm not sure the cagey response does much. If Scion 2e is a great game and needs to get there by shedding the ST lineage? I'll probably still love it. But I don't want to find that out when it gets a Kickstarter or when I get the book. If I'm expecting a variation on the ST system core and I get something that's pretty different even if I can see the ST influence, it will negatively prejudice my enjoyment of Scion. Which would suck.<br /> <br /> The sooner we know where to calibrate our expectations, the more time any initial dissonance has to abate before we get to see the final product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T14:17:22-08:00","id":15624,"title":"","content":"Oh, i just figure it's too early to say anything at this point. Probably most everything is being fiddled with. It's likely that something like &quot;you have 10 willpower&quot; would count at this point.<br /> <br /> I'm actually quite happy to hear that they are in heated discussions over it. It means there is a lot of awareness that there were bad things, and that is good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T17:46:47-08:00","id":15744,"title":"","content":"Yeesh. I wish you good health, Mr. Carriker. Glad to know this is being worked on by people who love the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T04:50:21-08:00","id":16049,"title":"","content":"I just recovered from my own spinal issues - I wish you the best on that front. I am eager to see the finished product, but do not kill yourself in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T18:40:10-08:00","id":16396,"title":"","content":"Glad to hear of your recovery. As someone still trying to wrap his head around the current system, a reworking of the system is extremely welcome, and as a major mythology nerd, I'm just HYPED that there'll be 10+ pantheons this time around.<br /> <br /> Things I have my fingers crossed for in 2e include Demeter and Hestia being included in the Dodekatheon (and Pan, if you're not dead-set on keeping his role from 1e), the Atzlanti, Amatsukami and Loa getting their rosters filled in a bit more, and nagas being lesser immortals instead of titanspawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/990-maplesamurai","name":"MapleSamurai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar990_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T07:07:13-08:00","id":18386,"title":"","content":"It's great to have some news about this, I've been expecting it like crazy. My only question is about release: is there a tentative date for the game? Is there any chance we'll see it on 2014, or will it be longer?<br /> <br /> I wish you a good health.<br /> Regards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1350-majortotoro","name":"MajorTotoro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T07:30:00-08:00","id":18399,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/schedule/</a> says May. However, Trinity stuff is in August, and they are using the same base system. I would be somewhat surprised if it was on time in May, judging based on every other Onyx Path product that has been put out and it's initial timeline. Scion has already been pushed back once <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I think there is a pretty good chance we'll see the Kickstarter by May, but the book will be a bit later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T11:37:47-08:00","id":18553,"title":"","content":"Any 2014 date is good news for me.<br /> <br /> One more question I'd like to leave here for any Developer passing by... Lots of questions here about the system, but I wonder how they are approaching the Setting. Scion 1E (are we calling it that?) was very lite on a Setting per se, just some pre-gens, hints here and there and several inconsistencies (like the Giant's <i>Masquerade</i> of sorts). Is the new Edition going to have more of a defined setting or is it going to go the old way with just stating what the game's premise implies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1350-majortotoro","name":"MajorTotoro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T22:48:08-08:00","id":18964,"title":"","content":"Sort of a mix, from what I've picked up. There'll be a core of setting-agnostic stuff, and then multiple settings to choose from (at least four, from what Joe's said elsewhere).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T12:28:43-08:00","id":22508,"title":"","content":"Wow. Thanks for the effusive welcome, folks, and for the well-wishes on my health. Much appreciated. I'm going to try and answer all of the actual questions posted. Wish me luck. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=14896#post14896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you share any thoughts you have on Fate and Fatebinding?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the mechanics behind Fatebinding are really closely tied to the new systems we're playing with and how they function, I want to hold off talking about the mechanics thereof for the moment. I will say, however, that our aim is to re-empower Fatebinding. It's such a cool concept, but mechanically it almost never comes up in the early stages of Scion 1e. I will also say that the intention is to put the power of its invocation into the hands of the player (though not the character, per se), so that who and what the character becomes Fatebound to help build the player's idea of his character's progress towards godhood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Man in Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=14937#post14937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to say that really like the concept of Touchstones, it is useful from a myth making and game stand point and isn't what everyone immediately imagines when playing Gods, my players were expecting to go to the Underworld and to the Overworld, but got really happy to find the Touchstones and after a while using them to travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! They're one of my favorite pieces of work, honestly. I find the occult principles of sympathy and contagion fascinating, and always wanted to find a way to work them in as a setting concept. I feel like Touchstones are my best effort at doing so to date. I also feel like they give us one of the best &quot;mythological stuff in the modern world&quot; vibe, as well - nothing like Carhenge to really create a weird amalgamation of our world with an older concept of the classical world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Man in Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=14937#post14937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, can you tell us anything about the general guide lines that are defining Scion 2? Like what is the relevance of Fate (narrative tool vs. mechanic tool)? How do you intend to convey the feeling of playing a God (are Epics and their crazy success scale still a thing)? Any change to the Metaphysics of the game (concerning places like Underworlds, Godrealms, Titanrealms, the influence of the Parent God and Pantheon....)? Are we going to be able to take what was given for Scion 1 and transfer it to Scion 2 (assuming that players will reach Demigod and God stages before the actual books cover it)?</div> </div> </div> </div>We are fairly dramatically changing the system. In point of fact, it's safe to say that it's a new system that is deeply inspired by (and includes certain Sacred Cows) of the old systems that provided the foundations for Scion 1e. To address your individual questions, though: Fate is very relevant (see answer above). We are extremely cognizant of creating a system that scales well, first and foremost, without going into a realm of basically non-playable-ness.<br /> <br /> As far as the cosmology of the setting, we will be playing with its concepts a bit - I find the old system a bit too homogenous. In order to fit some of the mythological locales into the first edition, we kind of had to crowbar some of them into Overworld or Underworld concepts, to their detriment (Guinee comes to mind immediately). I'd like to be a bit more respectful of the original cultures and bodies of myth in our movement forward, while still maintaining a playable game in which it is possible for those myths to all be simultaneously true (even if its only in a potent, Legend-infused mythological way).<br /> <br /> Part of our intentions with this edition is to give everything a good going-over. We've got a lot more room in the books to do this with, as we're excising the use of super long &quot;front of book&quot; fiction, and putting all of our core rules into the Scion: Origins core book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=15584#post15584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm expecting a variation on the ST system core and I get something that's pretty different even if I can see the ST influence, it will negatively prejudice my enjoyment of Scion. Which would suck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Expect something recognizeable at its baseline (it uses d10s in a pool, against a Target Number, character sheets covered in dots). We're being careful to avoid change for change's sake; that said, it is a new system. Its intentions are different, on some level, and it is intended to do different things (specifically, many of the core details are in place to allow a relatively smooth scaling from &quot;dude with gun and badge&quot; all the way to &quot;GOD OF JUSTICE&quot;). My goal with this system is simple: I want people to be able to take elements that are familiar to them from our previous edition and related games, and use them in a system that explicitly supports the kind of stories this system is intended to tell. That's going to mean some change, but I have a lot of faith in the folks doing the work on this system. I do hope that folks can set aside expectations and interact with the system as it is, rather than as they expect it to be. Let's be honest - having to somehow intuit the expectations of our fan-base when they hear the words &quot;Scion Second Edition&quot; is a bit above my paygrade.<br /> <br /> You will recognize a lot. Your dice pools are Attributes + Skills. You have a Legend stat. You have Virtues. There are Purviews. There are Boons. But every single one of these elements works a bit differently. We've changed up some of the names of those Traits, so that people don't make assumptions from previous editions about how they work. There are also some slick new mechanics that complement and enhance all of these things as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=18964#post18964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sort of a mix, from what I've picked up. There'll be a core of setting-agnostic stuff, and then multiple settings to choose from (at least four, from what Joe's said elsewhere).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is correct, yes. I like the sort of &quot;foggy setting&quot; of Scion 1e. It let me build the settings of my own games in such a way that they were very different things in their execution.<br /> <br /> That said, I also recognize that frankly not everyone has the time to do both setting-building *and* prepare for a game. Not these days. So we're also providing a handful of settings in the Scion: Hero book, *as well as* some in the Scion: Origins book, all intended to introduce places for players to romp around in with their characters created using those books. Without committing to doing so, if folks like any of these settings well enough, we may very well do future PDFs that further detail them, or PDFs with a couple of new settings as well. That kind of thing.<br /> <br /> Scion Second Edition is basically intended to be a &quot;myth engine&quot;, and we want some cool worlds in which to set those myths. So that's what we're doing with it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks, all, for your well-wishing, but most of all for continuing to love this game as much as we do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Regards,<br /> Joseph D. Carriker<br /> -------------------------------------------<br /> \u201cIn Springtime, O Dionysos, To thy holy temple come,<br /> To Elis with thy Graces, Rushing with thy bull-foot, come,<br /> Noble Bull, Noble Bull\u201d<br /> \u2015 Plutarch","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1242-jdcarriker","name":"JDCarriker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T13:05:06-08:00","id":22534,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Sounds like Epic Attributes might have gotten cut, as those weren't mentioned.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how to feel about that. While it was a balance issue at times, it's one of the things that made Scion work, IMO. Or it could have just not been mentioned (I mean, vampires still have potence, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T13:06:42-08:00","id":22536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...while still maintaining a playable game in which it is possible for those myths to all be simultaneously true (even if its only in a potent, Legend-infused mythological way). </div> </div> </div>So who put the stars in the sky, then? :P<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.gunnerkrigg.com/?p=1120\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.facebook.com/tr?id=560616780737475&amp;ev=PixelInitialized\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.gunnerkrigg.com/?p=1120\" target=\"_blank\"> Gunnerkrigg Court - Page 1120 - By Tom Siddell </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.gunnerkrigg.com/?p=1120\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.gunnerkrigg.com/?p=1120 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Gunnerkrigg Court is a science-fantasy webcomic created by Tom Siddell. It is updated online three days a week. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T13:10:16-08:00","id":22537,"title":"","content":"I'm really hoping they draw very heavily from how Aberrant handles its powers, because Aberrant seemed to inspire a lot of how Scion worked... but then the Scion designers were like &quot;Balance? Pfft. No one needs balance.&quot; And that was sad. Aberrant's Quantum Powers seem a lot more balanced with Mega Attributes than Scion's Epics and Boons. Scion1 <i>clearly and heavily</i> favors Epic Attributes. They give you <i>free</i> Knacks (a whole separate power system that often mimicked or replaced Boons), <i>geometrically increasing automatic successes</i> and they also <i>determine how good you are at your Boons</i>. Plus, you can Associate with an Epic at Legend 9, but need Legend 12 to Associate with a Purview.<br /> <br /> But then, I have a lot of hopes for Scion2. Since I'm not the developer, it clearly won't match my hopes exactly, but I'm still optimistic it will be playable and awesome so that every time someone wants to run a game of Scion, they don't have to <i>re-write the entire thing</i>. They do currently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T13:13:33-08:00","id":22540,"title":"","content":"Eh, I'm hoping that crafting isn't 'NPC only until you hit God'.<br /> <br /> That totally sucked for about half my players in my first game. I basically had to totally ignore it and just make it 'have to have above human skill/attributes' to craft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T15:44:17-08:00","id":22663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=22537#post22537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scion1 <i>clearly and heavily</i> favors Epic Attributes. They give you <i>free</i> Knacks (a whole separate power system that often mimicked or replaced Boons), <i>geometrically increasing automatic successes</i> and they also <i>determine how good you are at your Boons</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not forget that, if you don't want to buy the extra dot in the Epic Attribute, that you can just buy the Knack for 5 xp. WAY cheaper than Levelx5 for a new Boon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1311-woody-spider-deacon","name":"Woody Spider Deacon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T16:19:35-08:00","id":22694,"title":"","content":"Could you tell us anything about Birthrights? Are they going to be significantly different? And, most of all, are Creatures and Followers going to be relevant past Legend 4?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T18:38:30-08:00","id":22794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=22540#post22540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I'm hoping that crafting isn't 'NPC only until you hit God'.<br /> <br /> That totally sucked for about half my players in my first game. I basically had to totally ignore it and just make it 'have to have above human skill/attributes' to craft.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have strong mixed feelings about this issue.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, it would make little sense to say that a Scion cannot grant Boons from a Purview until he has boons of ranks 1-10 in that Purview, yet allow that Scion to build items that mimic those Boons. (I can't give them to my flesh and blood, but I can give them to inanimate objects? really?)<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it feels silly to suddenly say, &quot;I've ascended and I'm the god of crafting&quot; when you've never been able to build anything beyond the mundane up to that point. (let alone the fact that it isn't very fun for the players)<br /> <br /> Also... I'm not sure if it was intentional or not, but it felt like the Greeks were given a bit of an advantage. There were certain items that said things like, &quot;you must have Arete(craft) to build this&quot; or &quot;you must have Arete(marksmanship) to use this&quot;. Admittedly, I was just skimming, but it felt like Greeks had an advantage on Relics.<br /> <br /> But, back to the issue at hand... I agree that it would be nice if lesser Scions from any pantheon with the appropriate skills and Boons could craft Relics, and if the power of the Relics they could craft scaled with their Legend / Boons / Skills / something.<br /> <br /> Limiting the creation of Relics to forge/creation/whatever gods doesn't feel balanced, or true to the myths. There certainly seem to be too many deities who don't have artifice as a Purview, yet are able to create items, for this to make sense. Requiring Scions to pick and choose Boons from some forge/artifice/whatever Purview, or allowing the ability to create Relics to all Scions with the appropriate relevant stats (Sky 1-4 for a 1-dot sky relic, for example) seems to be the false dichotomy of choice.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like the idea of Scion ability to craft Relics starting at improving items (weapons with +1 damage or extra range, or armor with lower fatigue, for example), and slowly scaling to being able to grant access to Purviews, replicate Boons, and even more fantastic abilities at the high end.<br /> <br /> Of course, from what I skimmed, it looked like Scion ability to create non-magical items scaled faster and better than their ability to create magical items (IIRC, &quot;Concept to Execution&quot; gave some DCs for some truely incredible feats of science fiction, but I don't have the books in front of me).<br /> <br /> To cut to the chase, oh powers that be, has granting the ability to craft Relics before the average game is over even been talked about by the design team, and, if so, can you shed any light on how it might be balanced or scaled?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1311-woody-spider-deacon","name":"Woody Spider Deacon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T18:43:16-08:00","id":22795,"title":"","content":"I pray to to to higher power of your choice that the Devas and Celestial Bureaucracy are in 2e<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">and that the Allied/Yankee pantheons are utterly obliterated and never mentioned again</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T19:49:43-08:00","id":22841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=22795#post22795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I pray to to to higher power of your choice that the Devas and Celestial Bureaucracy are in 2e<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> Devas, as the word's largest polytheistic pantheon in terms of worshippers, BETTER BE","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T20:57:23-08:00","id":22876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woody Spider Deacon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=22794#post22794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, back to the issue at hand... I agree that it would be nice if lesser Scions from any pantheon with the appropriate skills and Boons could craft Relics, and if the power of the Relics they could craft scaled with their Legend / Boons / Skills / something.<br /> <br /> Limiting the creation of Relics to forge/creation/whatever gods doesn't feel balanced, or true to the myths. There certainly seem to be too many deities who don't have artifice as a Purview, yet are able to create items, for this to make sense. Requiring Scions to pick and choose Boons from some forge/artifice/whatever Purview, or allowing the ability to create Relics to all Scions with the appropriate relevant stats (Sky 1-4 for a 1-dot sky relic, for example) seems to be the false dichotomy of choice.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like the idea of Scion ability to craft Relics starting at improving items (weapons with +1 damage or extra range, or armor with lower fatigue, for example), and slowly scaling to being able to grant access to Purviews, replicate Boons, and even more fantastic abilities at the high end.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no mixed feelings on this. Scions ought to be able to do so, but I don't think we're necessarily talking about item CREATION here. We're talking about correctly binding an item's legends to it.<br /> <br /> No reason that the first tier of this process shouldn't be open to Heroes. Which is, in my estimation, ascribing true events to a particular item (Patton's quill, for example). Demigods could start lying about an item's provenance, essentially &quot;borrowing&quot; the legend of other items for their own (Excalibur or the Spear of Destiny). Gods would be the ones simply producing relics whole cloth for use by Scions and other gods -- essentially what craft gods do; bypassing the need for heroic things to have been achieved by an item of similar description in favor of simply infusing it with the pantheon's spare mojo.<br /> <br /> I like this sort of method better than most because it means something mundane that a Scion happens to carry with them for years can become a very powerful relic simply by its association with them. Gifts from the folks are nice, but something whose legend you built? You're going to be proud to hand that off to your kid someday. Even if it looks like a ratty Led Zeppelin t-shirt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T21:03:31-08:00","id":22879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=22795#post22795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">and that the Allied/Yankee pantheons are utterly obliterated and never mentioned again</span></div> </div> </div> </div>My group had a lot of fun with them. I'd like to see them return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T07:50:07-08:00","id":23754,"title":"","content":"My own questions to the powers that be:<br /> <br /> Will Scion 2e have concepts like the battle wheel, action speed, etc? I'm only just starting to play Scion 1e, but I have always liked systems with strong concepts of different actions taking different amounts of time. The system presented in Scion 1e seems much easier to use and much more &quot;playable&quot; than most such variable action time systems I have seen. I am hoping that the same attention to fun and game balance that seems prevalent in discussions of Scion 2e has gone into determining what will fill the role that the battle wheel filled in Scion 1e / that the Join Battle system has grown along with the rest of the system, and not simply been imported without evaluating the impact the new system will have on it.<br /> <br /> Will the dot ranges in Scion 2e be similar to the dot ranges in Scion 1e? In particular... I am hoping that divine beings can have greater Abilities than their mortal counterparts. It felt odd to me that a god of art was only better at painting than a mortal because he was more agile than a skilled mortal, a god of knowledge can have no more knowledge, only be smarter than a mortal, etc. Unless, of course, the god is Greek. Unless this done on purpose, to make the Greek gods feel special, as the only ones better than mortals, it would be nice to see that change in Scion 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1311-woody-spider-deacon","name":"Woody Spider Deacon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T05:03:05-08:00","id":24295,"title":"","content":"<b>Glad to hear that you are getting better! Keep us posted with tasty bits that make us salivate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T02:48:19-08:00","id":25019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raleel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=22879#post22879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> My group had a lot of fun with them. I'd like to see them return.</div> </div> </div> </div> Where is my dislike button.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T03:33:10-08:00","id":25028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=22537#post22537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really hoping they draw very heavily from how Aberrant handles its powers, because Aberrant seemed to inspire a lot of how Scion worked...</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that both Scion and the Trinity Continuum are getting overhauled, I wouldn't bet on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T12:31:48-08:00","id":25296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=25028#post25028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given that both Scion and the Trinity Continuum are getting overhauled, I wouldn't bet on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the same base system, no less!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 12-07-2013, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T13:34:42-08:00","id":25323,"title":"","content":"I guess it depends on how complete the overhaul is, but I still hope the new system takes a bit more inspiration from Aberrant than it does from Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T18:33:45-08:00","id":25481,"title":"","content":"Please no WWII pantheons in the core. Unless the game is drastically different they could be home brewed pretty easily. if that's not an option, maybe a web extra or something like a companion. Putting them in the core will only serve to detract from a unified &quot;children of ancient deities in the modern world&quot; theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T23:51:58-08:00","id":25629,"title":"","content":"I like the national Pantheons as part of the game. As I've said before, one of the things they do is help think of what Scions that grew into their own Pantheon rather than joining their parent's might end up building.<br /> <br /> That said, I definitely don't think they should be in the first books. There's plenty of room for another Companion or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T02:01:36-08:00","id":25685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=25629#post25629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the national Pantheons as part of the game. As I've said before, one of the things they do is help think of what Scions that grew into their own Pantheon rather than joining their parent's might end up building.<br /> <br /> That said, I definitely don't think they should be in the first books. There's plenty of room for another Companion or the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. From what's been revealed about 2e so far, pantheons now form at Demigod level. Having the national pantheons be examples of Demigod-level pantheons somewhere along the line could work... (It'd address one of the problems people who didn't like them had - that they were being put on the same level as the core pantheons - because now they wouldn't be.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 12-08-2013, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T06:20:14-08:00","id":25766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=25323#post25323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it depends on how complete the overhaul is, but I still hope the new system takes a bit more inspiration from Aberrant than it does from Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be surprised if any powers worked the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T06:25:02-08:00","id":25769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=25685#post25685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm. From what's been revealed about 2e so far, pantheons now form at Demigod level. Having the national pantheons be examples of Demigod-level pantheons somewhere along the line could work... (It'd address one of the problems people who didn't like them had - that they were being put on the same level as the core pantheons - because now they wouldn't be.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did this info come from? I'm curious now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T08:04:36-08:00","id":25792,"title":"","content":"Right here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=481#post481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but they'll be complete <i>settings</i> in their own right, even if they're not complete rulesets. <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ideally, Hero will be both a full mode of play and the first third of a heroic cycle, and a discussion on how your life changes when your blood turns to ichor. Demigod will build on that foundation, but will also be a full game in its own right. Our goal is to clean, build and expand upon the experience of the first edition of Scion, with Origin underlying the entirety of the line and providing a setting and mechanical backbone so we don't have to explain it all in Hero.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Origin</b><br /> <br /> We're still largely deciding what goes into Origin and what goes into Hero, but the idea is that the bare bones of the mechanical system will be laid out in Origin. <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The book can be used to create and play urban fantasy stories, and will include the setting(s) for doing just that. If creatures are handled in the book, they'll be beings of myth but low Legend - dryads, satyrs, and the like. And, yes, pre-Visitation Scions, but also holy men and women of the pantheons, sorcerers who seek to steal the power of the gods, and those bound by Fate (your Oedipuses, your Cassandras, your Arjunas). Some of its mechanics will include not just the baseline rules, but also rules for things that cross over and access all three tiers of play - magic and Fate among them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Hero</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hero will include rules on taking characters from the SCR and giving them their first dot of Legend, with all the powers and Purviews that come with that. Not having to cram a full rule-set into this book means that we've got more space in which to play with things, including a nice, fat variety of powers, and other elements that are Hero-specific. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is also where you'll see the full mechanical concept of our scaling system, which affects all four books. Moo hoo hah hah!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It also means that we've got space for a big catalog of pantheons, since the basics have been covered in Origin. The original six are returning (though we're talking about heavily changing the Loa), </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">going into more depth than Hero 1e did.</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> I'll ask him if we can spoil the rest (since we're talking about more). Ideally, Joe would like to touch on multiple other pantheons per book.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Demigod</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Demigod will include rules for bringing our heroes into the Divine tier, including the ability to Invoke their...well, that'd be spoiling too much. Suffice it to say what we're talking about includes stuff on how pantheons are formed, <i>what </i>pantheons actually are, and an exegesis of stuff like <i>interpretatio romana</i>. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It's definitely going to contain rules for play in mid-to-high Myth locales, such as Touchstones, Terra Incognita and the like, as well as Underworlds; and, of course, demigod powers. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b>God</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rules for bringing our heroes into the Empyrean tier, with all the power and responsibilities that assumes. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">More material for play in high-Myth locales, particularly Titan-Realms and Firmaments. And, yes, rules to shake the cosmos and the foundations of Fate.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T07:48:44-08:00","id":26498,"title":"","content":"Pantheons are comprised of gods and demigods (and culture heroes who exist on the hero level, but they don't do much, metaphysically speaking). When I mentioned them forming, I didn't mean to imply you, Jane Hero Smith, weren't part of a pantheon on the Hero level - you are. Demigod addresses how pantheons form as social as magical constructs within Fate, but you benefit from those constructs at every level, Origin included.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T12:31:52-08:00","id":27393,"title":"","content":"Will there be an official addition of the much fan-ruled concept of gathering legend/power from your own cult/followers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T12:49:00-08:00","id":27419,"title":"","content":"Hindus would love that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T13:00:16-08:00","id":27438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=27393#post27393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be an official addition of the much fan-ruled concept of gathering legend/power from your own cult/followers?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope not. It gets into that post-modern idea that humanity creates the Gods with their prayers and turns the Gods into divine politicians, hustling for mortal favor. That can be cool in a game <i>about humans</i>, but not in a game about Gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T14:04:26-08:00","id":27517,"title":"","content":"I think it would be uncool if having a cult/followers turns into a mandatory source of power. However making a cult/followers be meaningful seems like it would be just fine for a game about gods. Some gods are portrayed as being much more concerned with veneration than others. If there's an adequate &quot;balance&quot; of bonus and drawback such that it becomes a stylistic choice, I don't see what it hurts.<br /> <br /> Cults are pretty important in the new Mummy game, but they don't turn Mummies into divine politicians. So there are ways to handle this that avoid that particular issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T21:58:19-08:00","id":27761,"title":"","content":"So how much money do I need to throw at you guys to ensure that Eric/Donnie/Etc will be used for the example characters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T23:50:56-08:00","id":27808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=27517#post27517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be uncool if having a cult/followers turns into a mandatory source of power. However making a cult/followers be meaningful seems like it would be just fine for a game about gods. Some gods are portrayed as being much more concerned with veneration than others. If there's an adequate &quot;balance&quot; of bonus and drawback such that it becomes a stylistic choice, I don't see what it hurts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, although I use mortals for Fate in my games more than for Legend. But I have been giving legend points to my PCs for participating in \u00abfateful events\u00bb or going towards the fates ... they got from mortals ; )<br /> <br /> Then again, I mostly wing it, because 1ed didn't efficiently answer these issues.<br /> <br /> But since this is about 2e, I'll go ahead and ask:<br /> <br /> -In which book will the metaphysics be adressed? (nature of Ichor, Titans, Gods, metaphysical difference between overworlds, terra incognita, underworlds, the World) I had mixed feelings with the \u00abfoggy setting\u00bb. It did leave me room to create my own answers and keep my Occult PC wondering, but sometimes I also felt alone to deal with these issues. Even if there was a cannon answer, as an ST I can change or adapt material as I see fit for my campaign, so it wouldn't be a game breaker to give a bit more information.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, I also recognize that frankly not everyone has the time to do both setting-building *and* prepare for a game. Not these days. So we're also providing a handful of settings in the Scion: Hero book, *as well as* some in the Scion: Origins book, all intended to introduce places for players to romp around in with their characters created using those books. Without committing to doing so, if folks like any of these settings well enough, we may very well do future PDFs that further detail them, or PDFs with a couple of new settings as well. That kind of thing. </div> </div> </div>-Campaign builder. Just wanted to point out that I would enjoy those campaign setting ideas that was mentionned. I feel a good Storyteller section would enhance Origins a great deal. What themes to dig? PROs and CONs of Single-pantheon vs Multi-pantheon Band? How to create enthralling Social and Mental challenges to give those PCs a time to shine? Pre-Visitation and Visitation explained and expanded.<br /> <br /> I actually thought the Storyteller section in 1ed was good (except mechanics) but too short. The 2-book perspective of Origins / Hero is interresting in that regard.<br /> <br /> -Oh and... Mass Combat? I've come up with my own simple system to leave the spotlight to the PCs while making clashing armies important and meaningful (creating fast and easy mechanics to favor Mental characters for strategy, Socials for morale and leading troops in the fray). I found the rules regarding mass battle in Companion confusing at best, long crunchers at worst. Is there something in 2ed for epic battles?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1625-papy","user":"Papy","date":". 12-11-2013, 03:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1625-papy","name":"Papy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T08:21:15-08:00","id":27988,"title":"","content":"Mass Combat would be good, yeah. Not much point in playing a War god without it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T11:27:13-08:00","id":28137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=27988#post27988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mass Combat would be good, yeah. Not much point in playing a War god without it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humbly disagree, but in general I've found most RPG mass combat systems to be nothing but disappointing. I don't know if I want to see a lot of developer effort on something every table is probably going to house rule or ignore, depending on their particular tastes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T12:53:07-08:00","id":28221,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see a mass combat system, but it shouldn't take up space in either the mortals book or the Hero one. For one, you can't build that sort of system until you've at least got the rules for demigods hammered out. Also, it's usefulness at lower levels is pretty slim.<br /> <br /> And, as always, if it doesn't strike my fancy I'll use something else. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T03:12:50-08:00","id":28607,"title":"","content":"So...ten pantheons. Well, if the main five from the first edition will be in there, and add the Devas for good measure, then there's four pantheons up for grabs. If we add the Atlantean pantheon in there, then we can have the Seven Wonders series as inspiration for the game. Also, I would like to see Pan be a good guy. I was saddened to see that Pan was a villain because I thought it would be cool to be a scion of Pan and call the satyrs brothers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T05:19:06-08:00","id":28644,"title":"","content":"No Atlanteans please. It'd be nice to stick to actual Pantheons from real cultures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T06:12:46-08:00","id":28672,"title":"","content":"Yeah.<br /> <br /> I'd like a Companion or splat that focuses on 'Creating Your Own Pantheons!' that can have as examples the Atlanteans (sigh...), Yankee (uurgh...), Allied (uuuurrrrrghhh...) etc. for those that did like those options as well as a focus on being able to create Pantheons from the hundreds of cultures out there to steal from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 12-12-2013, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T07:01:22-08:00","id":28693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woody Spider Deacon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=22663#post22663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's not forget that, if you don't want to buy the extra dot in the Epic Attribute, that you can just buy the Knack for 5 xp. WAY cheaper than Levelx5 for a new Boon.</div> </div> </div> </div>My Scion of Huitzilopotchli actually worked this out in-character to some degree. The rest of my group started grabbing Boons while he was working on increasing his physical strength (I built him as a kind of Venom styled parkour commando) and after about 3 months of game time he was seriously underwhelmed by their magic tricks. Out of character, I don't think more than one or two Boons were ever used to any worthwhile effect in our entire 2 year long game. Epic Attributes (especially with the Knacks) were incredibly powerful, didn't require a relic/birthright to make use of them, and for the most part cost nothing to activate. Add to that the fact that virtually all of the Boon powers sucked or did something totally useless... I think my Scion had 4 in addition to the ones he started with, and only ever used two of them.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Frankly, my main concern for Scion 2 is that Scion 1 appeared to be mainly written by people who'd never tried to actually play it. The example characters were pretty bad at their intended specialties, the mechanics didn't remotely reflect what the fluff appeared to be attempting to create, etc etc.<br /> <br /> Just as a for-instance, one of the 'combat' characters in the Demigod book had no Epic Stamina. Not very little, none. And IIRC, no Epic Dex. She'd have been a smear in the first round of combat with most of my group back in their Hero days, let alone at higher Legend.<br /> <br /> It would also be nice if ranged combat is a viable option this time around. I created a character who refused to use guns (prior to reading the rules all the way through) because I was trying to limit him, and it turned out being a matter of refusing to use a completely useless weapon because guns or even bows are utterly worthless in the old system.<br /> <br /> <br /> I really really liked the idea of Scion, and I'd love to see the new edition overcome the failings of the old, but I'd be lying if I said I wasn't a bit concerned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T07:50:40-08:00","id":28725,"title":"","content":"The only consistently useful Boon powers I've seen from evaluating 'well how often will that come up in a game?' in the RAW, despite never playing it, are some of the spells in Magic, or the first level stuff for Earth, Sky, Fire and Frost (which grant Immunity).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T10:30:23-08:00","id":28803,"title":"","content":"A fairly common house rule added Perception to damage for ranged weapons (sometimes also to hit). It worked well in our group. Would be nice to see it make its way into 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T10:30:39-08:00","id":28804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=28607#post28607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...ten pantheons. Well, if the main five from the first edition will be in there, and add the Devas for good measure, then there's four pantheons up for grabs. If we add the Atlantean pantheon in there, then we can have the Seven Wonders series as inspiration for the game. Also, I would like to see Pan be a good guy. I was saddened to see that Pan was a villain because I thought it would be cool to be a scion of Pan and call the satyrs brothers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, there're six main pantheons in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T11:59:42-08:00","id":28860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=28644#post28644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No Atlanteans please. It'd be nice to stick to actual Pantheons from real cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>This can't be said often enough. There are more than enough Pantheons from actual cultures. There's no need to make them up to fill the core rulebooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T12:26:39-08:00","id":28877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=28860#post28860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This can't be said often enough. There are more than enough Pantheons from actual cultures. There's no need to make them up to fill the core rulebooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm. It wasn't just to fill space, but also as part of the core chronicle (a long-hidden secret of the gods that now becomes a way to make contact with the Overworld).<br /> <br /> More generally, the 1e writers' view of the game appears to have differed in one key respect from the view that took hold in the fandom - the writers appear to have been seeing it as a game of the children of the gods, but the fandom came to see it as a game of the children of the gods of religion and myth. Resulting in the Atlanteans, and in the vehement reaction to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T13:32:37-08:00","id":28897,"title":"","content":"It is, admittedly, the view of the game I was sold on before I finally looked into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T14:46:06-08:00","id":28944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=28644#post28644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No Atlanteans please. It'd be nice to stick to actual Pantheons from real cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet the story of Atlantis was a part of Ancient Greek and Egyptian mythos (thanks to (Plato? Aristotle?). Hell, there's an Atlantis tv series which starred Greek legends like Hercules in there. I feel the NOT having an Atlantean pantheon in the game would be unkind to the people who told about the ancient city-nation in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T15:31:53-08:00","id":28964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=28944#post28944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet the story of Atlantis was a part of Ancient Greek and Egyptian mythos (thanks to (Plato? Aristotle?). Hell, there's an Atlantis tv series which starred Greek legends like Hercules in there. I feel the NOT having an Atlantean pantheon in the game would be unkind to the people who told about the ancient city-nation in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Atlantis is Poseidon's demesne according to Critias in his interview with Plato. Its kings are scions of his line. It's hard to fathom (no pun intended) why they would have a pantheon markedly different from the Dodakatheon, except perhaps that Poseidon is their most important god.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T16:59:09-08:00","id":29008,"title":"","content":"Yarrr. Atlantis isn't a whole different culture, its just a fancy magical island of the Greeks and it only appears once, ever, in a single story told by Plato as an allegory. There's no myths about it, no legends, just one allegory. Its only modern people that have taken it as a &quot;real&quot; place, mostly because of spiritualism in the early 20th century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T18:21:04-08:00","id":29058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=28964#post28964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Atlantis is Poseidon's demesne according to Critias in his interview with Plato. Its kings are scions of his line. It's hard to fathom (no pun intended) why they would have a pantheon markedly different from the Dodakatheon, except perhaps that Poseidon is their most important god.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've hit it on the nose, my friend.<br /> <br /> Like everyone else, I am glad to hear of 10 pantheons coming with Hero. I would hope to see our 'core six' plus the Tuatha, Devas, Celestial Bureacracy, and probably say the Babylonian gods (since they set the tone for a lot of myths to come), because one issue with the Companion featured Pantheons were that they got very little screen time and detailing beyond their respective sections. Pretty much even the other rules and setting oriented other Companion parts roundly ignored their existence (and their respective Titans).<br /> <br /> My hope is this time around you can devote plenty of time and space to giving each Pantheon and all good thorough spotlights and flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1654-the_gm","name":"The_GM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T19:06:16-08:00","id":29083,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Atlanteans and their city can be cast as pantheon that split off from the main dodakatheon or at least a city founded by scions that eventually fell to corruption. The only way that could be more Greek is if they started [redacted].","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T22:44:54-08:00","id":29164,"title":"","content":"If they wanna use Atlantis or the National Pantheons for something like examples of PC-created Pantheons, that's fine. Those <i>will</i> be fictional and that's cool. Just don't make them a major playable faction and take space away that could have been used for the Hittites or Cherokee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T22:52:55-08:00","id":29167,"title":"","content":"As long as they do thorough research when they decide to add a pantheon, I'm happy.<br /> <br /> And yeah, there are plenty of pantheons of polytheistic faiths to draw from - there is no need for a Yankee pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1659-kenright","name":"kenright","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T23:01:00-08:00","id":29169,"title":"","content":"Yes, I can't agree with you more. There isn't a need for a Yankee Pantheon at all. I don't even want to see an example one <br /> <br /> [ATTACH=CONFIG]n163[/ATTACH]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T23:56:26-08:00","id":29183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kenright</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=29167#post29167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as they do thorough research when they decide to add a pantheon, I'm happy.<br /> And yeah, there are plenty of pantheons of polytheistic faiths to draw from - there is no need for a Yankee pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>We do not know in what capacity the people at <a href=\"http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/\" target=\"_blank\">Gotham By Night </a>have been involved, but there are quite a few of us who are crossing our fingers and hoping they are involved in fact checking and researching the pantheons to be as accurate as such things are capable of being.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T05:43:36-08:00","id":29260,"title":"","content":"The Dynamic Duo from Gotham are heavily involved. Verisimilitude and mechanical needs come before accuracy, but accuracy is still a high priority, if that makes sense. Of course, I'm speaking for myself and my writing, not for Joe or OP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 12-13-2013, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T07:37:43-08:00","id":29295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=29260#post29260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Verisimilitude and mechanical needs come before accuracy, but accuracy is still a high priority, if that makes sense. Of course, I'm speaking for myself and my writing, not for Joe or OP.</div> </div> </div> </div>It definitely makes sense. The primary goal is to make a game that is fun to play and mechanically balanced; the mythology comes second because there will always be people like John and Anne who will correct the mythology after the game is published.<br /> <br /> But if you have experts who are willing to help you get the mythology right the first time? If they will make sure the mythology is as accurate as possible within the mechanical framework required by the game? <i><b>That is the best option of all.</b></i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T09:03:43-08:00","id":29352,"title":"","content":"I think a key reason for trying to get the mythology accurate is that for many many many people their prime exposure to these foreign and new pantheons/cultures/etc. will be games like this.<br /> <br /> Getting it <i>seriously</i> wrong can cause all kinds of confusion and potential trouble for people to learn stuff.<br /> <br /> I was much the same with, for example, the Loa. I knew <i>nothing</i> about them before Scion (not that they even existed) and after reading Scion 1e Core that was the full extent of my knowledge. With the Greek or Norse stuff I coudl tell what was fiddled and tweaked as I knew a lot of it anyway...but for the new stuff?<br /> <br /> Yeah...not great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T11:27:51-08:00","id":29429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=29260#post29260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dynamic Duo from Gotham are heavily involved. Verisimilitude and mechanical needs come before accuracy, but accuracy is still a high priority, if that makes sense. Of course, I'm speaking for myself and my writing, not for Joe or OP.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not one I find unreasonable, although I say this with trepidation. Nobody is perfect and there are still readily identifiable compromises in nearly every pantheon -- but those compromises are only apparent to people with a more extensive knowledge base in pagan tradition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T14:42:43-08:00","id":29539,"title":"","content":"World Mythology is infinitely complex and does not lend itself to being shuffled neatly into a box where everything is the same. Myths aren't balanced, aren't designed to be played through as a game with a mechanical system. They're stories, and they're not even necessarily concerned with internal consistency <i>within the same story</i>, much less within the hundreds or thousands of years that the society existed who worshipped them. Stories that are concerned with getting across a point that illustrates a philosophical or religious tenant, generally. Trying to write a game that accurately reflects all of world mythology is crazy. It won't be balanced. It will need a different system for every single mythological creature, and often multiple conflicting systems for the same mythological creatures.<br /> <br /> I totally understand that accuracy is important, but a functioning game can't be so concerned with accurately representing or explaining every single myth and story that it forgets <i>it's a game</i> and it needs <i>balanced rules</i> and systems that are fairly <i>elegant</i>. It can try to come up with the most balanced and elegant system that it can, while keeping a maximum amount of flexibility. It can include accurate information <i>in so far as it goes</i> on the mythic figures included. But it's going to have to make calls and work things into the framework of the game's own internal mythology. <br /> <br /> There's no need to go making things up just to fit holes, like the Drowned Road, or get things objectively wrong for no good reason, like Crom Cruach, or shoehorning in weird suicide-bomber-angels that serve the Egyptian Sun Titan... but it's pretty silly to try explaining every single weird thing every single God does, ever, in terms of mechanics. They're Gods and they've got Stories To Tell. Sometimes they're just gunna break the rules. That's fine. They do that. The game can't, because if you just toss the rules out the window, you're back to &quot;I killed you!&quot; &quot;No you didn't!&quot; &quot;Yes I did!&quot;. You can give the players some rule-bending with effects that turn mechanical conflicts into narrative ones, like Ultimate Attributes and Boons, but they still have to follow the rules. No one is using Ultimate Death to create a new species of animal, or cure a plague, or re-ignite the frozen sun. No one is using Ultimate Appearance to lift a mountain and turn it upside down into a floating island.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T06:02:40-08:00","id":29858,"title":"","content":"Oh I'm not complaining about the need for switchig stuff up for mechanical needs.<br /> <br /> My main issue is that as a lay person my only exposure to 'voodoo' gods was the Loa as presented in the Scion 1e. And that presentation makes no mention I can remember of Yoruba or how it's not a pantheon in the same sense as the Greeks or the nuances between how the gods are structured or whatever. That's stuff that could all be done with descriptive text that would not <i>need</i> - but could benefit from - mechanical representation. It would primarily need someone who knows their stuff to cast a critical eye over the flavour text.<br /> <br /> If the text piques interest then I'll start searching for more info. But if I don't even have any idea what a 'Loa' is why would I go looking for them? Or even know of the word 'Loa' in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T08:20:49-08:00","id":29920,"title":"","content":"I loved the Original Scion, unsable rules and all. I have run 4 different games and they all (with a lot of house rules) went great! I do think that playtesting is very important and will hopefully be done to a large degree. It was weird when ever my players would make a character and only a few games in were way better Scions than the examples in the books. At least at doing what they were supposed to do. I loved the example fluff for the most part also.<br /> <br /> The things I had issue with were- I didn't like that most boons were kinda worthless. I usually had to come up with inventive ways to intice players to get more of them when Epic attributes and knacks were the real power in the game. The creation of Birthrights was kinda weak. We had fun coming up with items because luckily my groups were fun and imaginative, but I would definately like some more hard and fast rules for that aspect. I thought Arete, while fluffy was a bit unfair to the other pantheons sometimes. I would like to see more fluff or maybe systems that explain or help explain how the world reacts to the scions? Obviously the Vatican would be a tad upset if the scion of Thor was on the Tonight show joking around with Jay. I loved Ragnarok, but felt it was limited by only being a book for the Norse. I understand why and still wedged my guys into it without much problem, but it would be cool to see that kind of book embrace other Pantheons. I liked the Fluff for Atlantis a great dead but rarely was anyone interested in playing a scion from there. While I loved rolling eight hundred dice the first few games, it gets a little old after a while. Maybe instead of adding more and more dice, maybe lowering the difficulty every so often. I could roll 18 dice looking for 7 ups or roll 5 dice looking for 6 ups or something. Or maybe 10s are more powerful on different teirs. I would like more Evil/ corrupted Scion options. I loved the action wheel for initative order, please keep that. I would like maybe some mention or mechanics of faith in respect to how people are nowadays. In other words, Thor is cool, but peoples worship of money is probably more powerful than half the gods combined.<br /> <br /> <br /> I will post more when I can think about it or talk to my players, but am super excited about this and cannot wait!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1528-hivemind","name":"Hivemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1528_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T12:21:47-08:00","id":30038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=29260#post29260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dynamic Duo from Gotham are heavily involved. Verisimilitude and mechanical needs come before accuracy, but accuracy is still a high priority, if that makes sense. Of course, I'm speaking for myself and my writing, not for Joe or OP.</div> </div> </div> </div>This leaves me ecstatic! I've been using their site for additional boons, and missing pantheons for years. Even if you just copy all the additional boon powers they present it'll more than double the range of abilities each purview has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T21:58:30-08:00","id":32159,"title":"","content":"I'm going to have to be the odd duck out, because I liked the Atlantean Pantheon and did not mind the 'national pantheons' for the WWII section of Companion. Trying to paint that it would force them to not work on minor pantheons like the Cherokee is a bull shit supposition. A fallen pantheon that was 'scrubbed' from history is a cool idea, showing that even gods or whole pantheons can fall or be destroyed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T23:04:29-08:00","id":32187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=32159#post32159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to have to be the odd duck out, because I liked the Atlantean Pantheon and did not mind the 'national pantheons' for the WWII section of Companion. Trying to paint that it would force them to not work on minor pantheons like the Cherokee is a bull shit supposition. A fallen pantheon that was 'scrubbed' from history is a cool idea, showing that even gods or whole pantheons can fall or be destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you've got only so much money to devote to a project and it's pages, that money should not be given to fictional pantheons. You want pantheons scrubbed from existence? Try the Spanish Gods, or the Arabian Gods, or any one of the Germanic gods that got wiped out when the Romans went through Gaul like a tiger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T23:38:35-08:00","id":32199,"title":"","content":"Oh I'd love to see something on the pre-Roman Gods of Spain/Iberia. I know essentially nothing but a few stubs on Wikipedia about them, dead and gone, vanished into history but th epeople's who worshipped them contended with Carthaginian and Roman invasions, so maybe some interesting bleeding over of traditions and deities from both of those groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T02:02:31-08:00","id":32234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=32159#post32159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to have to be the odd duck out, because I liked the Atlantean Pantheon and did not mind the 'national pantheons' for the WWII section of Companion. Trying to paint that it would force them to not work on minor pantheons like the Cherokee is a bull shit supposition. A fallen pantheon that was 'scrubbed' from history is a cool idea, showing that even gods or whole pantheons can fall or be destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have no fear. You're not actually alone in this. I get why most Scion fans want more focus on actual real world Pantheons and all, but I liked the books introducing other options. Having the existence of fictional or non-religious Pantheons in the game material doesn't mean you can't play a strictly mythology based game and it does mean those of us more interested in a looser concept of myth-based stories can have some fun too.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, there's no actual limit to the number of books Scion can get beyond demand and interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T09:34:49-08:00","id":32479,"title":"","content":"I have no particular opinion on the Atlantean one, but I rather liked the WW2 one. We used it to great effect in our game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T20:45:56-08:00","id":32936,"title":"","content":"The Yankee/Soviet/French/Britannia type pantheons certainly have a place in Scion. I think the write-ups they got in Companion may not be accurate for a modern game, and probably weren't even all that accurate for a historical game. However, I think Nationalism, Economics, Monotheism, and such-like as Pantheons makes a heck of a lot of sense. Econ would be a huge pantheon, with Gods/Demi-Gods/Scions of Capitalism, Socialism, Communism, Free Market, Mass Media, Commerce, etc. Nationalism could have a single deity to represent the &quot;spirit&quot; of each country. Even the &quot;Pantheon&quot; of Monotheism could work, since most monotheists believe we are all &quot;children of God&quot; (For example, a Scion of the Christian Father could have the ichor infused via Baptism or something.)<br /> <br /> OR if it's too controversial, ignore/forget about the idea of a &quot;Pantheon of Monotheistic Deities.&quot; But I think having &quot;Modern Gods&quot; is not a bad idea at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1112-sprunka","name":"sprunka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T01:12:05-08:00","id":33006,"title":"","content":"The idea is that your Scions <i>are</i> those modern gods. They just haven't become Gods yet. Scion doesn't work like American Gods, where belief creates more Gods. If it did, sure, there'd be Media and the Web-Spider along with Uncle Sam and Mother Russia. Instead, it's about the ancient Gods having kids that will grow up and become modern Gods. If someone wants their PC to become Uncle Sam, totally cool. Uncle Sam just won't exist prior to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T02:16:52-08:00","id":33020,"title":"","content":"Can we stop with the bashing of the fictional/national Pantheons?<br /> <br /> It's a preference. Some people like them, some people don't. They weren't a part of the core books before and I haven't seen anyone on the &quot;like&quot; side of things demand that they start getting included there in 2e. Liking them also doesn't mean that you don't &quot;get&quot; what Scion is supposed to be about.<br /> <br /> We can save stoking the flames for after the development team finishes the essentials of the game and has time to start thinking about supplements that will address playing around with the various widgets and elements that make the game up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T02:16:56-08:00","id":33021,"title":"","content":"I think a book ike Mirrors for Scion would work, offering alternative ideas for pantheons, including a setting where the spirits of countries rather than cultural pantheons are the ones who bestow powers, or one where Scions draw power from the elements","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T03:14:58-08:00","id":33039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=32187#post32187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you've got only so much money to devote to a project and it's pages, that money should not be given to fictional pantheons. You want pantheons scrubbed from existence? Try the Spanish Gods, or the Arabian Gods, or any one of the Germanic gods that got wiped out when the Romans went through Gaul like a tiger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there actually enough known about those pantheons for them to create a reasonable accurate portrayal of them as opposed to making stuff up and putting their name on it? Serious question, I don't know much about the subject.<br /> <br /> And even if they do have enough, I think using the Atlantean pantheon alongside them would be a good idea. When people think about a wondrous lost society they think about Atlantis, using the gods of the really well known lost city as an example of a lost pantheon that has fallen out of power just seems like a really good way to grab attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T04:22:59-08:00","id":33063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=33039#post33039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there actually enough known about those pantheons for them to create a reasonable accurate portrayal of them as opposed to making stuff up and putting their name on it? Serious question, I don't know much about the subject.<br /> <br /> And even if they do have enough, I think using the Atlantean pantheon alongside them would be a good idea. When people think about a wondrous lost society they think about Atlantis, using the gods of the really well known lost city as an example of a lost pantheon that has fallen out of power just seems like a really good way to grab attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't thought about Atlantis since college, or at the very least the last time someone bemoaned Indiana Jones and the Fate of Atlantis not being a movie yet. It's...actually hard to tell which at this point.<br /> <br /> I've thought a lot about Ur and the Sumerian pantheon, though. Probably because I had just finished up Islamic studies courses and was hip-deep in Abrahamic mythology and the Sumerian flood myth appealed to my more banal side.<br /> <br /> We know enough about the Ibero-Gallic gods that the Gallic side has already received a pantheon. We know quite a bit about the Arab idols since they didn't really fall out of favor until around 800AD or so. We know a ton about the Germanic pantheons. While study of our polytheistic roots doesn't get much play or a lot of attention in the United States (primarily because the US never had polytheistic roots) there's a lot of really exciting work being done in the field in the Scandinavian, Celtic, Gallic, and Germanic parts of the world. The religious practice of paganism in all its flavors is, if I remember correctly, the only form of religious engagement actually growing in Europe right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T06:32:22-08:00","id":33133,"title":"","content":"Neither the Atlanteans nore the Yankee or other created pantheons bothered me. I bought the WWII book because of them not despite them. They were <i>new</i>, and I wanted to read the creativity that went into them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sprunka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=32936#post32936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Yankee/Soviet/French/Britannia type pantheons certainly have a place in Scion. I think the write-ups they got in Companion may not be accurate for a modern game, and probably weren't even all that accurate for a historical game. However, I think Nationalism, Economics, Monotheism, and such-like as Pantheons makes a heck of a lot of sense. Econ would be a huge pantheon, with Gods/Demi-Gods/Scions of Capitalism, Socialism, Communism, Free Market, Mass Media, Commerce, etc. Nationalism could have a single deity to represent the &quot;spirit&quot; of each country. Even the &quot;Pantheon&quot; of Monotheism could work, since most monotheists believe we are all &quot;children of God&quot; (For example, a Scion of the Christian Father could have the ichor infused via Baptism or something.)<br /> <br /> OR if it's too controversial, ignore/forget about the idea of a &quot;Pantheon of Monotheistic Deities.&quot; But I think having &quot;Modern Gods&quot; is not a bad idea at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something about this bugs the piss out of me, but I think it's probably because there's more truth here than is warranted for a game.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, there are a lot of others places that can be thrown in for &quot;creation;&quot; Lyonesse, Ys, Cimmeria, Hyperborea, Shamballah, Thule, El Dorado..etc...most of which I'm sure would follow many other pantheons that are known. But it's what's not known, that we can play &quot;fill in the blanks with other gods and stuff.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T16:33:42-08:00","id":33524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=33006#post33006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea is that your Scions <i>are</i> those modern gods. They just haven't become Gods yet. Scion doesn't work like American Gods, where belief creates more Gods. If it did, sure, there'd be Media and the Web-Spider along with Uncle Sam and Mother Russia. Instead, it's about the ancient Gods having kids that will grow up and become modern Gods. If someone wants their PC to become Uncle Sam, totally cool. Uncle Sam just won't exist prior to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uncle Sam could have been a Scion that already ascended...likewise for Media, Mother Russia, The State, etc. If we, as players, can create the next generation of Gods, there is no reason that there couldn't have risen an intermediate generation. Not out of belief and followers, but out of a desire to exemplify those things that people already believe in. And no, I don't think neo-Pantheons need to be in the core books, but I would *love* to see, and would definitely buy, a neo-Pantheon supplement.... perhaps a PoD/Digital only small book[let] per pantheon, or a compilation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1112-sprunka","name":"sprunka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T19:05:26-08:00","id":33629,"title":"","content":"That's true, but part of what I like about Scion is that the Gods are <i>just now</i> coming back. That this generation of Scions is the first in hundreds or thousands of years. You're new, different, craaazy! No one knows what you'll become! This is <i>the game</i> of special snowflakes. It takes some of that away if all the cool, modern stuff is already done. What is there left for your PCs to become if someone is already Media and the Web-Spider and Mother Russia and The Almighty Dollar? You get left with whatever wasn't cool enough to get written about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T06:57:40-08:00","id":33833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=32159#post32159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to have to be the odd duck out, because I liked the Atlantean Pantheon and did not mind the 'national pantheons' for the WWII section of Companion. Trying to paint that it would force them to not work on minor pantheons like the Cherokee is a bull shit supposition. A fallen pantheon that was 'scrubbed' from history is a cool idea, showing that even gods or whole pantheons can fall or be destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don\u2019t need to go to purely fictitious Pantheons to get the \u201cfallen Pantheon\u201d thing. I\u2019d much rather see something like the Gaelic or Arabian Gods as evidence that even whole pantheons can be destroyed than promoting a fragment of Greek Mythology into full Pantheon-hood. <br /> <br /> OTOH, I wouldn\u2019t mind if 2e\u2019s <b>Scion: God</b> used something like the Yankee Pantheon as an optional illustration of founding a new Pantheon \u2014 though even there, I\u2019d want an overhaul that treats it as a synthetic Pantheon founded primarily by gods of more traditional Pantheons who immigrated with their followers. <br /> <br /> Conversely, I can do without the Allied Pantheon: lumping together British, French, and Russian figures of myth does not make for anything resembling a coherent Pantheon; and I\u2019d much rather have separate Welsh, Gaelic, and Slavic Pantheons than a one-note \u201cnon-American WWII Allied Nations\u201d Pantheon. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T07:09:01-08:00","id":33836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=33629#post33629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true, but part of what I like about Scion is that the Gods are <i>just now</i> coming back. That this generation of Scions is the first in hundreds or thousands of years. You're new, different, craaazy! No one knows what you'll become! This is <i>the game</i> of special snowflakes. It takes some of that away if all the cool, modern stuff is already done. What is there left for your PCs to become if someone is already Media and the Web-Spider and Mother Russia and The Almighty Dollar? You get left with whatever wasn't cool enough to get written about.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I\u2019d like to see a line drawn between what the <i>writers</i> do with <b>Scion</b> and what they leave up to the <i>gamers</i> to do. In my view, the writers should stick to providing gameable representations of real-world myth and legend, plus providing the tools that the gamers will need to make something new out of that: focus on the foundation and the tools, and leave the rest of the construction up to us. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T09:36:47-08:00","id":33911,"title":"","content":"Quibbling over the fate of the non-historic pantheons is a waste of all our times. IF they include them, they only need to place them in their own book like they should have done the last time, which then allows the rabid supporters to buy that book (netting Onyx Path a tidy profit) while the fanatical detractors can cheerfully ignore it. As long as it isn't continually referenced as part of the setting canon such as it is, then this would be a double-win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T18:16:00-08:00","id":34203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=28804#post28804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Er, there're six main pantheons in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops. Thanks. Had a brain fart since I made that post around midnight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T18:21:11-08:00","id":34207,"title":"","content":"Quote from Neall: &quot;The Dynamic Duo from Gotham are heavily involved.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's proof in The Adventures of Batman and Robin where Batman meets &quot;Zeus&quot; and the Olympian mistakes Batman for Hades. lol. :-D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T18:32:23-08:00","id":34212,"title":"","content":"Quote from Heavy Arms: &quot; Originally posted by <b>ArthurHansen</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=32159#post32159\">View Post</a><br /> I'm going to have to be the odd duck out, because I liked the Atlantean Pantheon and did not mind the 'national pantheons' for the WWII section of Companion. Trying to paint that it would force them to not work on minor pantheons like the Cherokee is a bull shit supposition. A fallen pantheon that was 'scrubbed' from history is a cool idea, showing that even gods or whole pantheons can fall or be destroyed.<br /> Have no fear. You're not actually alone in this. I get why most Scion fans want more focus on actual real world Pantheons and all, but I liked the books introducing other options. Having the existence of fictional or non-religious Pantheons in the game material doesn't mean you can't play a strictly mythology based game and it does mean those of us more interested in a looser concept of myth-based stories can have some fun too.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, there's no actual limit to the number of books Scion can get beyond demand and interest. &quot;<br /> <br /> Thank You! And for the people who said that Atlantis was a Grecian fantasy. According to what I know, the Egyptians also talked about Atlantis back in Ancient Times. The Greeks were the first to pen the theory. If the Atlanteon Pantheon isn't going to be one of the main ones, then they may want to do what they did in Scion: Demigod and recreate the adventure where the Scions rediscover the Lost Pantheon and the Scions that they made without anyone finding out. Since, the Greeks and Egyptians discussed the nation of Atlantis, there may be other cultures like the Aztecs and the Scions of the Loa who also have ancient tales of Atlantis, thereby leading into a global discussion between all the known pantheons. Atlantis may very well be a hidden pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T19:22:00-08:00","id":34233,"title":"","content":"I think someone should use the term &quot;Onyx Path&quot; for a place of Gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T20:23:18-08:00","id":34263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=34212#post34212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank You! And for the people who said that Atlantis was a Grecian fantasy. According to what I know, the Egyptians also talked about Atlantis back in Ancient Times. The Greeks were the first to pen the theory. If the Atlanteon Pantheon isn't going to be one of the main ones, then they may want to do what they did in Scion: Demigod and recreate the adventure where the Scions rediscover the Lost Pantheon and the Scions that they made without anyone finding out. Since, the Greeks and Egyptians discussed the nation of Atlantis, there may be other cultures like the Aztecs and the Scions of the Loa who also have ancient tales of Atlantis, thereby leading into a global discussion between all the known pantheons. Atlantis may very well be a hidden pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure you're not thinking of how Plato claimed that the Egyptians described Atlantis as so and so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T21:21:21-08:00","id":34285,"title":"","content":"This. The only known story of Atlantis came through Plato, a greek philosopher who may very well have made it up out of whole cloth. Mind you, the Greeks weren\u2019t the only ones who had legends of an ancient civilization that rose to greatness and was then destroyed practically overnight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T22:39:01-08:00","id":34309,"title":"","content":"It wasn't really a legend as much as Plato creating a &quot;what-if&quot; scenario for a teaching point. And the other ancient Greeks understood that. Atlantis was not a story they told, like they told the story of Icarus, or the Minotaur or Narcissus or Echo. It was something Plato made up to illustrate a philosophical point in an essay. This was well understood until the early 20th century when spiritualists read about it, said &quot;cool!&quot; and turned it into a big thing with their whole whacky ideas about the secret history of the world. And now it's a Western pop-culture thing.<br /> <br /> Most of the other people with stories of ancient civilizations are <i>actually talking about other civilizations</i>. The Aztec told stories about Tollan, but today experts are fairly sure that Tollan was a mythed-up version of one or more real pre-Aztec civilizations kinda mushed together into one single mythic place. That kinda thing. There's tons of magical islands with all kinds of cool stuff on them, but in Scion terms those are Terra Incognita.<br /> <br /> I would <i>love</i> to see Atlantis as a Terra Incognita. As a <i>Greek Story</i>. But not as a made-up civilization lost to the mists of time. Don't need all that jazz because practically anything you invent in your imagination for an ancient society? Real history has an ancient society <i>doing that, but cooler</i>. People, man, they do weird stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T00:47:57-08:00","id":34345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=34309#post34309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would <i>love</i> to see Atlantis as a Terra Incognita. As a <i>Greek Story</i>. But not as a made-up civilization lost to the mists of time. Don't need all that jazz because practically anything you invent in your imagination for an ancient society? Real history has an ancient society <i>doing that, but cooler</i>. People, man, they do weird stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a worthy point; I wouldn't belittle people for a lack of understanding regarding Atlantis. Plato was an exceptional storyteller, having learned at the knee of the Socrates; indeed, given perspective and a significant training in the humanities, it's fairly clear that Atlantis is another exercise in the Socratic method, albeit on a much larger scale. Opening with the conjecture that is beyond logical answer to teach the student that there are going to be moments when logic fails and faith must dictate your response.<br /> <br /> Atlantis as pseudo-myth is fine territory to tread; a Scion of Poseidon could spend a large portion of his career trying to re-discover Atlantis and that would strike me as perfectly acceptable. I just fail to see the need for an imaginary pantheon derived from exactly no authoritative source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T01:05:24-08:00","id":34347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=34345#post34345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just fail to see the need for an imaginary pantheon derived from exactly no authoritative source.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking games here. &quot;Need&quot; is likely too strong a word.<br /> <br /> The desire for an imaginary pantheon derived from exactly no authoritative source in a game? Well that's simple. Existing real world pantheons have inherent baggage. You can gloss over and white-wash plenty, but if you're dealing with the Norse mythology in your game, you have to deal with their concept of fatalism on some level. A fictional pantheon lets you pick and choose what you're dealing with by using that pantheon without any of the issues of feeling like you're being completely unfaithful to the cultural basis of a real-world one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T04:52:25-08:00","id":34895,"title":"","content":"The problem i had with National Pantheons (i put aside Atlantean one, because it bothers me, but not SO much) is that they feel like a mockery of real pantheons. They destroy all the sense of epicness. You are thinking about being a mighty son of Horus, or Tezcatlipoca,or whoever. And then you hit a Scion of Uncle Sam. Pecos Bill. The Citizen. <br /> <br /> And wait a second, because they are on the same level as Dyonisus, Bastet, Baron Samedi. <br /> <br /> What. The. Fuck. There can't be enough facepalms about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T05:39:36-08:00","id":34905,"title":"","content":"And that's not even bringing up Betsy Ross. Sewing a flag, no matter how amazing, should not put you on the same level as Kali.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T07:19:04-08:00","id":34935,"title":"","content":"*boggle*<br /> <br /> It doesn't make sense to me that age is more of a factor than current worship. If this is the case, then the Loa must seem as children to certain pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":". 12-22-2013, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T08:10:13-08:00","id":34942,"title":"","content":"Most of the Loa are plenty ancient, from back in the day in Yorubaland when they were the Orisha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T08:11:18-08:00","id":34944,"title":"","content":"You know, my group had a scion of Robin Hood, of John Bull, and of Uncle Sam along side one of shiva and one of Odin. They did just fine. Sure, Betsy Ross isn't going to be the same feel of epic that a goddess of death has, but neither is a pacifist goddess of fertility or a number of other completely inappropriate comparisons to a multiarmed goddess of death. My own group stormed Dieppe and was the only successful part of that. We tracked down the shield of Joan of arc. In the process we shoved a scion of Hephaestus into the gut of a jotun, rescued 500 prisoners from a prison in the middle of Germany, blew up a scion of Vidar using subterfuge, lying, and sleight of hand, smuggled those 500 soldiers by hook or by crook to Amsterdam, through the sewers and got them on a stolen transport ship out of said port, sabotaging our likely pursuit. Then we got chased by a soul-eating destroyer manned by zombies that transformed into a giant robot right in the middle of the English Channel. And we still got the 500 prisoners home for Queen and country. Every last one. So, ya, I feel like it can be pretty damned epic. If you don't like it, that's fine. I played the scion of Odin in that mess, so it's not like I don't get it, but everyone else had a blast and felt their characters. I'd like to not take that from them and dismiss it and diminish it and tell them that they are not epic. Let's drop the No True Scotsmen arguments and just accept that folks like to play it different. I have little doubt they'll put it in a different book anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T08:16:02-08:00","id":34945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=34935#post34935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*boggle*<br /> It doesn't make sense to me that age is more of a factor than current worship. If this is the case, then the Loa must seem as children to certain pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Yoruban gods, in one incarnation or another, have been around for thousands of years and are one of the longest running religions around. If you want to point the finger at a rather young pantheon then you can aim it squarely at the Teotl, though even they have plenty of loan figures from other nearby pantheons that are much older.<br /> <br /> But either way you swing it, current worship should not be a viable metric for determining the strength of a pantheon. At best you can use it as a vague measuring stick for determining Legend, on the grounds that pantheons that have been forgotten are probably not Legend 12.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T08:29:06-08:00","id":34947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raleel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=34944#post34944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, my group had a scion of Robin Hood, of John Bull, and of Uncle Sam along side one of shiva and one of Odin. They did just fine. Sure, Betsy Ross isn't going to be the same feel of epic that a goddess of death has, but neither is a pacifist goddess of fertility or a number of other completely inappropriate comparisons to a multiarmed goddess of death. My own group stormed Dieppe and was the only successful part of that. We tracked down the shield of Joan of arc. In the process we shoved a scion of Hephaestus into the gut of a jotun, rescued 500 prisoners from a prison in the middle of Germany, blew up a scion of Vidar using subterfuge, lying, and sleight of hand, smuggled those 500 soldiers by hook or by crook to Amsterdam, through the sewers and got them on a stolen transport ship out of said port, sabotaging our likely pursuit. Then we got chased by a soul-eating destroyer manned by zombies that transformed into a giant robot right in the middle of the English Channel. And we still got the 500 prisoners home for Queen and country. Every last one. So, ya, I feel like it can be pretty damned epic. If you don't like it, that's fine. I played the scion of Odin in that mess, so it's not like I don't get it, but everyone else had a blast and felt their characters. I'd like to not take that from them and dismiss it and diminish it and tell them that they are not epic. Let's drop the No True Scotsmen arguments and just accept that folks like to play it different. I have little doubt they'll put it in a different book anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstand me...how epic a Scion is has nothing to do with their parent. Look at Achilles, second only to Hercules as far as Greek heroes are concerned. His mother is more famous for being his mother than for any exploit of her own. That didn't stop him. And yet I would still take issue with someone claiming that Thetis is on the same level as Athena.<br /> <br /> My concern with Betsy Ross (and really, most of the Pantheons in World at War) is not that she is a different kind of epic than Kali, but that she's not epic period.<br /> <br /> By comparison, Isis is Kali's complete opposite, but she's still just as legendary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T08:31:41-08:00","id":34948,"title":"","content":"And to clarify, it was not my intention to belittle your group's accomplishments. I was simply putting forth my opinion as to why I do not think the National Pantheons fit well into Scion's landscape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T08:31:50-08:00","id":34949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=34905#post34905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's not even bringing up Betsy Ross. Sewing a flag, no matter how amazing, should not put you on the same level as Kali.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially since it's pretty much a known fact that she didn't even actually sew the flag. Ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T10:52:58-08:00","id":35012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=34948#post34948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was simply putting forth my opinion as to why I do not think the National Pantheons fit well into Scion's landscape.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with your stated position is that Scion does not treat all god-level beings as equals. Just because Uncle Sam and Kali shouldn't be equals in your estimation, doesn't mean they can't both be god-level characters in Scion; because the gods in Scion still have a scale and hierarchy.<br /> <br /> There's also the issue of Scion, and to an extent real world mythology, don't really care much about age or worship levels for apotheosis. In the span of a single human life time (less even) Heracles went from infant to Olympian. The game itself is built very much on that trajectory. A player character is expected to be able to go from exceptional human (pre-visitation) to god (end of game level play) within a relatively short amount of time. If a player character can go from 1 to Kali's equal over the course of a game, why can't Uncle Sam do so over the course of 200 years?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T11:09:21-08:00","id":35017,"title":"","content":"The problem with the first point is that Gods in Scion can only have associated Purviews at Legend 12, after they buy the Avatar. Since every one of the National Pantheon Gods has Purviews associated, they are on the same level as Zeus and Odin, which is what I disagree with.<br /> <br /> As for the second, Hercules and Dionysus are very much exceptions to the rule. Few other Scions in world mythology approach Apotheosis. Now I agree that by the rules Uncle Sam could do just what you suggest, but then, by the same logic, the question arises, why hasn't Osiris learnt every single Purview in existence? He's definitely had the time for it by now. If we start giving out power levels and associations based on what Gods <i>could</i> have learnt by now instead of what they actually do in myth, then setting out lists of associated powers becomes meaningless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 12-22-2013, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T11:56:08-08:00","id":35042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35012#post35012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with your stated position is that Scion does not treat all god-level beings as equals. Just because Uncle Sam and Kali shouldn't be equals in your estimation, doesn't mean they can't both be god-level characters in Scion; because the gods in Scion still have a scale and hierarchy.<br /> <br /> There's also the issue of Scion, and to an extent real world mythology, don't really care much about age or worship levels for apotheosis. In the span of a single human life time (less even) Heracles went from infant to Olympian. The game itself is built very much on that trajectory. A player character is expected to be able to go from exceptional human (pre-visitation) to god (end of game level play) within a relatively short amount of time. If a player character can go from 1 to Kali's equal over the course of a game, why can't Uncle Sam do so over the course of 200 years?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the biggest and most obvious problem with the idea of Uncle Sam-as-deity is that historically he's never been worshiped. Nor has Paul Bunyan, or Pecos Bill, or any of the pseudo-nationalist figures in any of the made-up pantheons. This cheapens the overall nature of godhood and purview for some people, which can obviously have deleterious effects on their feelings toward the game.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that the Greeks had one of the most successful empires in history and as such would have to have had some of the most successful heroes in history. The patronage of their kings and war heroes tended to be re-attributed to a god if they became significantly great. Herakles was, by all accounts, significantly great. He sacked cities, married princesses, was a king, had 100 children, helped found a dozen more cities, and only the Christian cultists of the early eras bothered to try to squeeze all of this chronologically into a single human lifetime. The Greek sources are far less precise in measuring his period of activity.<br /> <br /> Greek heroes underwent apotheosis with startling frequency, particularly if they were successful in founding a major city (Hercules actually kind of stands out as the only one never to have founded his own city).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T13:00:32-08:00","id":35084,"title":"","content":"From Scion: Companion at the beginning of the World at War Section - <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you\u2019re feeling a little apprehensive about adding a historical setting to your game, we offer this simple advice: don\u2019t sweat the details. Nobody\u2019s going to test you on facts, you don\u2019t need to memorize any dates and your high school history teacher isn\u2019t going to grade your character\u2019s back-story. For most groups of players,<b> the fun will come from establishing the feeling of the war rather than from maintaining strict historical accuracy</b>\u2014and it\u2019ll be a lot easier that way, too.<br /> <br /> By the same token, <b>this section is not meant to deliver an accurate representation of the historical war</b>. World War Two is a vast subject which has been the focus of thousands of books, and there are simply not enough pages here to do justice to the real-life triumphs, catastrophes, heroics and horrors of the war. <b>Furthermore, this section presents an alternate history\u2014that is, history viewed through the lens of mythology.</b> Just as when playing in a modern setting, <b>Scion in the context of World War Two diverges from \u201creal life\u201d</b> as we know it to follow the epic tradition, complete with heroes who perform amazing deeds, villains with supernatural powers and pointy-toothed monsters that would happily munch on any of the above. </div> </div> </div>Bolding is mine, for emphasis.<br /> <br /> Seriously, it's not meant to be an accurate representation of history. So the fact that they are not worshiped is utterly irrelevant to them not appearing or Besty Ross never sewing a flag, nor her being on the same level as Kali. They literally made new myth out of it, and I think it's pretty cool. I totally get that it's not everyone's cup of tea, but to say it degrades Scion in some way is just simply a matter of opinion, and hardly universal. You don't like Vampire Dark Ages? don't use it. You don't like Forgotten Realms? Don't use it. Same here.<br /> <br /> I mean, seriously, how is 5 Scion commandos sneaking into a Nazi castle disguised as no less than Himmler, Goebbels, Hitler, and their personal guards (complete with guy who can only say Nein! in German) to rescue 500 POWs any less mythic than the Trojan Horse? How is a Scion of John Bull with a mystic bulldog (mystic mastiff?) named Winston ripping the hatch of a tank and leaping from ship to ship under heavy gunfire less awesome than Odysseus taking down a cyclops? How is scion of Uncle Sam named Ulysses Samuel Adams who can summon forth his own personal commandos with the flag over Fort McHenry braving the North Sea and the power of a Soul-powered ship with nothing but his red, white, and blue swim trunks to sabotage it mythic and legendary than Perseus taking down a Medusa? How is a Scion of Robin Hood dodging the bullets of 100 Germans and making an entire battlefield look at him so that the rest can get into position not the stuff of legends? Just because they don't have worshipers in the Real World for a fictional game?<br /> <br /> Maybe not in your world, but mine... totally happened, and awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T13:42:09-08:00","id":35099,"title":"","content":"You're dissembling; none of the scenarios posed could not be accomplished with the original six pantheons' Scions. Which is the point that has been made repeatedly. Not having made-up pantheons costs the game nothing and gains it quite a bite in credibility and acceptance from a plurality of players who are practicing pagans.<br /> <br /> I suppose I should frame it this way: how would you feel if people could just print up bachelor's degrees from your college and have them validated as just as real as yours? Not a perfect analogy, but close enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T13:43:42-08:00","id":35101,"title":"","content":"No one is saying you can't tell awesome stories with something like American Gods, or the WW2 &quot;Pantheons&quot;. No one is saying they can't be amazing, cool, badass and bitchin. That is not being said, suggested, implied or hinted. They ARE totally awesome, they CAN be totally badass and they can make for AMAZING stories. <br /> <br /> What IS being said is that they do not FIT into a game of Gods and Titans, where ancient myth has returned to the world and YOUR PC's (not some made-up fictional characters written by OTHER PEOPLE) are the heralds of modern myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T13:52:01-08:00","id":35103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35101#post35101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one is saying you can't tell awesome stories with something like American Gods, or the WW2 &quot;Pantheons&quot;. No one is saying they can't be amazing, cool, badass and bitchin. That is not being said, suggested, implied or hinted. They ARE totally awesome, they CAN be totally badass and they can make for AMAZING stories.<br /> <br /> What IS being said is that they do not FIT into a game of Gods and Titans, where ancient myth has returned to the world and YOUR PC's (not some made-up fictional characters written by OTHER PEOPLE) are the heralds of modern myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoted for emphasis","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T13:56:41-08:00","id":35105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=34945#post34945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Yoruban gods, in one incarnation or another, have been around for thousands of years and are one of the longest running religions around. If you want to point the finger at a rather young pantheon then you can aim it squarely at the Teotl, though even they have plenty of loan figures from other nearby pantheons that are much older.<br /> But either way you swing it, current worship should not be a viable metric for determining the strength of a pantheon. At best you can use it as a vague measuring stick for determining Legend, on the grounds that pantheons that have been forgotten are probably not Legend 12.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you guys are going to fit the &quot;this pantheon borrowed gods that are older&quot; then you are indeed saying age is a relevant factor.<br /> <br /> On a curious note, according to Robert Campbell, the oldest deity ever worshipped, was the bear. With the snake (I believe) coming in a close 2nd.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raleel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35084#post35084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, it's not meant to be an accurate representation of history. So the fact that they are not worshiped is utterly irrelevant to them not appearing or Besty Ross never sewing a flag, nor her being on the same level as Kali. They literally made new myth out of it, and I think it's pretty cool. I totally get that it's not everyone's cup of tea, but to say it degrades Scion in some way is just simply a matter of opinion, and hardly universal. You don't like Vampire Dark Ages? don't use it. You don't like Forgotten Realms? Don't use it. Same here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this.<br /> However to add that real-life myth making is ongoing. Hero-ification constantly runs throughout history. Most people in the US (my country btw) used to celebrate the myths surrounding Thanksgiving. Now many just give thanks on that day without those idiot pilgrims.<br /> <br /> George Washington, the god of war; Thomas Jefferson, the god of Life, Liberty, and the Pursuit of Happiness; Ben Franklin, the god of invention...and the list can go on. And yet, despite what we know of such individuals, good and bad, and perhaps more to the point, how very human they all were, we kind of do...worship them. We idolize them, their on every monetary unit, we create statues for them...kind of like what older beliefs did for their respective gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T14:36:41-08:00","id":35131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35017#post35017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with the first point is that Gods in Scion can only have associated Purviews at Legend 12, after they buy the Avatar. Since every one of the National Pantheon Gods has Purviews associated, they are on the same level as Zeus and Odin, which is what I disagree with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the problem is the mechanics, not the national Pantheons. As you yourself noted, you'd have a problem with a minor Greek god(dess) being on the same level as Zeus, but in Scion canon Persephone has associated Purviews and is therefore on the same level as Zeus and Odin.<br /> <br /> If the problem is that you don't want Uncle Sam to be as powerful as Zeus, then the simple thing is to remove the requirement that you need to be Legend 12 to have associated Purviews so that lesser gods don't all need to have Legend 12 just to have Scions that get associated Purviews. That addresses the much larger issue you've stated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Few other Scions in world mythology approach Apotheosis. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I agree with that assertion, but that is largely meangingless. The game is built around this assumption as being the primary path for the PCs: they'll achieve apotheosis and become gods. That's how the trajectory of the game is built. It's in the title of the books as clear as can be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we start giving out power levels and associations based on what Gods <i>could</i> have learnt by now instead of what they actually do in myth, then setting out lists of associated powers becomes meaningless. </div> </div> </div>I feel like you're shifting the goal posts here. Your complaint has never been that Uncle Sam has the specific Purview associations that he does and that they're just attributed poorly, your complaint is that he has them at all because of what rules say he must have done to have them. Since you agree he could have done what it takes to have them, the whole Osiris tangent seems entirely irrelevant. Both of them are written up in the rules based on what the authors felt was appropriate to the mythology around them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35042#post35042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the biggest and most obvious problem with the idea of Uncle Sam-as-deity is that historically he's never been worshiped.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last time I checked, worship is not actually required of deities in Scion. If worship is a requirement of high Legend, it screws with a few conceits of the game (plenty of the deities in the books that nobody is complaining about being there were rarely worshiped because of their associations; ex: Hades); for forces high level play into a very different modality than it has been presented as (since building a following of worshipers is not presents as a fundamental activity). You also get into a very sticky point regarding worship vs. veneration vs. secular mythology. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This cheapens the overall nature of godhood and purview for some people, which can obviously have deleterious effects on their feelings toward the game. </div> </div> </div>Conversely, sticking to an extremely rigid interpretation of mythology can remove the fun out of the game for people that just want to play and not research ancient mythology just to know what on earth is going on, which can obviously have deleterious effects on their feelings towards the game.<br /> <br /> There's also some pretty faulty thinking that goes into a line of thought that comes down to being invested in the game supporting only your preferred modality of play. When has a supplement introducing support for playing the game with a looser concept of core conceits actually harmed a game of people playing closer to the default premise of the game? Did the Scion Companion's national Pantheons ever actually ruin anyone's game by virtue of existing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35101#post35101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What IS being said is that they do not FIT into a game of Gods and Titans, where ancient myth has returned to the world and YOUR PC's (not some made-up fictional characters written by OTHER PEOPLE) are the heralds of modern myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this is that nobody has come up with a good reason as to why Scion can't handle both modalities of play.<br /> <br /> You're essentially arguing that because they do not fit into the Scion game you want, they don't fit into what Scion is or can be. Why does Scion have to be strictly limited to that one approach to the material? Why can't Scion be run with the national Pantheons arising and that being the impetus for the ancient Pantheons to get back in the game adding another level of conflict beyond Titan smashing? Why can't Scion be run with Legend being closer to American Gods in how it impacts mystical strength allowing for a greater mix of modern and ancient gods?<br /> <br /> Yes, using those element is silly if you want to just play ancient myth returning and the PCs being the fresh modern twist on it, but that doesn't mean these things can't coexist within the same RPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T14:42:34-08:00","id":35133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35099#post35099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're dissembling; none of the scenarios posed could not be accomplished with the original six pantheons' Scions. Which is the point that has been made repeatedly. Not having made-up pantheons costs the game nothing and gains it quite a bite in credibility and acceptance from a plurality of players who are practicing pagans.<br /> <br /> I suppose I should frame it this way: how would you feel if people could just print up bachelor's degrees from your college and have them validated as just as real as yours? Not a perfect analogy, but close enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>if they were just playing a game with them? I would not care one bit. It's a game, not a belief structure. There is a whole other avenue for that. If someone saying &quot;I play Scion, therefore I am an expert on Mythology&quot; or &quot;I play Scion, therefore I am a pagan&quot;, that is patently ridiculous. I'm not saying that, and I don't think you are either.<br /> <br /> Having the pantheon you don't like in another book doesn't really cost anything either, outside of book production, and that can stand or fall based on economics just as easily as anything else <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T14:44:47-08:00","id":35137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35017#post35017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with the first point is that Gods in Scion can only have associated Purviews at Legend 12, after they buy the Avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s certainly the way it works in 1e. I\u2019ve argued in the past for changing that in 2e, and allowing all Gods to have associated Purviews regardless of their Legend, as part of breaking free of the \u201clinear purchasing scheme\u201d mentality for Purviews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T14:47:12-08:00","id":35140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35101#post35101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one is saying you can't tell awesome stories with something like American Gods, or the WW2 &quot;Pantheons&quot;. No one is saying they can't be amazing, cool, badass and bitchin. That is not being said, suggested, implied or hinted. They ARE totally awesome, they CAN be totally badass and they can make for AMAZING stories.<br /> <br /> What IS being said is that they do not FIT into a game of Gods and Titans, where ancient myth has returned to the world and YOUR PC's (not some made-up fictional characters written by OTHER PEOPLE) are the heralds of modern myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Needless to say, I disagree. I think it fits just fine. Sure, it's not your image of the game, and that's fine too. I have no problem seeing it and how it works. I even think the story presented for the alternative history is actually not bad at all.<br /> <br /> I don't disagree that it's not really a main setting sort of thing for this. But disregarding as &quot;it doesn't belong&quot;? That's too narrow a view of myth and legend in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T14:55:21-08:00","id":35144,"title":"","content":"I've had this Argument with Telgar myself Raleel. Just let go and agree to disagree. You're not going to convince Telgar that anything from the era of indoor plumbing is Epic enough for Scion. Might as well be arguing how many angels are dancing on the head of this pin.<br /> <img src=\"http://4.bp.blogspot.com/-eqjeC580k60/UDTqB9IJkMI/AAAAAAAAB0M/ZT03cpv94M4/s1600/10009pin.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> But enough of this disgression, anyone know which books JDCarriker (Did I spell that right?) was on in Exalted 2e? I've can't remember seeing him around the Forums. And to keep things vaguely on topic, which books did he write for Scion 1e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T14:59:18-08:00","id":35149,"title":"","content":"If nothing else the modern ones can provide ideas for those PCs who prefer to move into some aspect of modern myth, and can be ignored easily enough otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T15:05:30-08:00","id":35155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35131#post35131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then the problem is the mechanics, not the national Pantheons. As you yourself noted, you'd have a problem with a minor Greek god(dess) being on the same level as Zeus, but in Scion canon Persephone has associated Purviews and is therefore on the same level as Zeus and Odin.<br /> <br /> If the problem is that you don't want Uncle Sam to be as powerful as Zeus, then the simple thing is to remove the requirement that you need to be Legend 12 to have associated Purviews so that lesser gods don't all need to have Legend 12 just to have Scions that get associated Purviews. That addresses the much larger issue you've stated.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I agree with that assertion, but that is largely meangingless. The game is built around this assumption as being the primary path for the PCs: they'll achieve apotheosis and become gods. That's how the trajectory of the game is built. It's in the title of the books as clear as can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you move the requirement without impacting the structure of the game itself? You pointed out yourself that the presumption is the PCs will achieve apotheosis; moving requirements around like that would drastically alter the trajectory of play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35131#post35131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last time I checked, worship is not actually required of deities in Scion. If worship is a requirement of high Legend, it screws with a few conceits of the game (plenty of the deities in the books that nobody is complaining about being there were rarely worshiped because of their associations; ex: Hades); for forces high level play into a very different modality than it has been presented as (since building a following of worshipers is not presents as a fundamental activity). You also get into a very sticky point regarding worship vs. veneration vs. secular mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your premise, e.g. that Hades was not worshiped, is facile on its face. It's also stupendously wrong and wrong-headed. The intent was not to delve into worship v. veneration; to wit, I would actually be surprised to learn that American children are aware of, much less venerate, figures like Pecos Bill or John Henry. Secular mythology is dangerous ground to tread; are we going to deify Bloody Mary? What about about The Candyman? Urban legends are an interesting place to look for inspiration for games, but there are plenty of other games that are willing to explore them. Some of them are even published by OPP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35131#post35131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversely, sticking to an extremely rigid interpretation of mythology can remove the fun out of the game for people that just want to play and not research ancient mythology just to know what on earth is going on, which can obviously have deleterious effects on their feelings towards the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>If anyone is actually sitting down to make an academic study of pre-Christian mythology in order to play this game, they deserve applause and not your ridicule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35131#post35131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also some pretty faulty thinking that goes into a line of thought that comes down to being invested in the game supporting only your preferred modality of play. When has a supplement introducing support for playing the game with a looser concept of core conceits actually harmed a game of people playing closer to the default premise of the game? Did the Scion Companion's national Pantheons ever actually ruin anyone's game by virtue of existing?</div> </div> </div> </div>What didn't get published in favor of the national pantheons? When you can answer that question, I won't have to answer yours.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35131#post35131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with this is that nobody has come up with a good reason as to why Scion can't handle both modalities of play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, as I pointed out above, there are several other games, published by OPP, that are not only capable of doing so but <u>intended</u> to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35131#post35131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're essentially arguing that because they do not fit into the Scion game you want, they don't fit into what Scion is or can be. Why does Scion have to be strictly limited to that one approach to the material? Why can't Scion be run with the national Pantheons arising and that being the impetus for the ancient Pantheons to get back in the game adding another level of conflict beyond Titan smashing? Why can't Scion be run with Legend being closer to American Gods in how it impacts mystical strength allowing for a greater mix of modern and ancient gods?</div> </div> </div> </div>We're asking the developers to stick with the game's core conceit, focus on improving that &quot;mission statement&quot; play style before exploring alternatives. We're asking because there are already games published by the same company designed to allow people to explore the alternatives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35131#post35131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, using those element is silly if you want to just play ancient myth returning and the PCs being the fresh modern twist on it, but that doesn't mean these things can't coexist within the same RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also doesn't mean that development effort should be spent on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T16:39:35-08:00","id":35197,"title":"","content":"The developer and writers have already said one of their goals for Scion2 is to have multiple &quot;settings&quot; for the game. The National Pantheons could be such a setting, that's fine. So could a steampunk civil war setting, or a space opera setting, or anything else. It's a little harder to shoehorn in something like American Gods where faith is the fuel for deities because that would need some kind of system and it'd be pretty fundamental to the game. That'd be much harder to work out as a setting-specific trait than just different takes on what Scion can be and do.<br /> <br /> When White Wolf pitched Scion, it was ancient mythology awakens in the modern days. That's what got me, and a lot of other people, to play it. That's why we've stuck with it when the system is laughable, the books are terrible and the writing is sub-par. That idea, of classical myth in the modern age, is <b>badass</b>. Is it the <i>only</i> badass thing that exists? No. Can other things be equally badass? Yes. But they are <i>not</i> what Scion was claiming it was about when it was released. That's not what we bought into. Can Scion be <i>expanded</i> to include other ideas? Sure, why not? It just needs to be clear that those things are an <i>alternate take</i> on Scion. You don't sign up for a Werewolf: the Apocalypse game and then get handed a pile of material for the Wild West. That's what Werewolf: the Wild West is for. You don't crack open a copy of Romeo and Juliet to read about the battle between the Capulet and Montague crime families of California. That's when you go watch Romeo+Juliet. <br /> <br /> CAN Scion be all these other things? Of course. But it needs to be itself first. It needs to deliver on its original promise: ancient myth in modern times. Then there can be all kinds of alternate settings and game mods and everything else. Those need to come <i>later, </i>and <i>after</i> they get the original game right. This isn't a case of saying that Pizza Hut must ONLY EVER SELL PIZZA, it's saying that maybe they should hold off on trying to sell pasta, salads, desserts and roast chicken until they <i>get pizza right</i>. Cause if your flagship concept can't sail, what's the point of spending time on all the extra stuff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T16:44:23-08:00","id":35198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35155#post35155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you move the requirement without impacting the structure of the game itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>By keeping it at god level without requiring Legend 12. Have alternate ways to be linked to a Purview besides buying the Avatar so that gods without Legend 12 and the Avatar for a Purview can still have associations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your premise, e.g. that Hades was not worshiped, is facile on its face. It's also stupendously wrong and wrong-headed. </div> </div> </div>I didn't say &quot;not worshiped&quot; I said &quot;rarely.&quot; Also calling something &quot;facile&quot; and &quot;wrong&quot; is kinda contradictory. Either I'm right but superficial in my point, or wrong, but I can't be both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If anyone is actually sitting down to make an academic study of pre-Christian mythology in order to play this game, they deserve applause and not your ridicule. </div> </div> </div>Where did I ridicule anyone?<br /> <br /> As well, I fully appreciate anyone that wants to put serious study into cultures and mythology. But Scion is a game; not an undergraduate class. I want to be able to sit down and play with people without restricting myself to classics majors, the well self-educated, and so on.<br /> <br /> If I'm going to run a game of Scion at a convention (I generally run 1-2 convention games a year), I need it accessible enough that people of all backgrounds can sit down and have a blast. Because that's more important to activity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What didn't get published in favor of the national pantheons? When you can answer that question, I won't have to answer yours. </div> </div> </div>Nothing didn't get published in favor of the national pantheons. It wasn't the last book of Scion 1e. If there was more to publish it would be been; or more likely was dropped due to the general dislike of Scion 1e's mechanics combined with the events that led to the creation of OPP and OPP buying Scion outright from CCP. As there was no announced new Scion material in the wings, even if the Scion 1e writers had things to pitch, they weren't getting through.<br /> <br /> I fail to see how this make my question not need answering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because, as I pointed out above, there are several other games, published by OPP, that are not only capable of doing so but <u>intended</u> to do so. </div> </div> </div>I don't see this as a sufficient answer. OPP makes two vampires games right now. OPP publishes the nWOD which has both a full vampire game, and a changeling game that includes vampric changelings.<br /> <br /> Overlap is both clearly something that doesn't impede product development, nor is it a particular concern for OPP.<br /> <br /> Also? OPP doesn't have a game about playing the children of mythological figures; both modern and ancient. It has games that can touch on that theme, but it doesn't have a game meant to be what Scion is with the national pantheons as a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We're asking the developers to stick with the game's core conceit, focus on improving that &quot;mission statement&quot; play style before exploring alternatives. </div> </div> </div>Some people are. Other people are asking the developers to never explore alternatives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It also doesn't mean that development effort should be spent on them. </div> </div> </div>It doesn't mean that effort shouldn't be spent on them. Development effort should be spent on what the developers feel are good things for the game; not just what a portion of the fans think is the most important part of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T19:19:17-08:00","id":35286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35198#post35198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some people are. Other people are asking the developers to never explore alternatives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the sheer amount of real-world mythology out there, the distinction between focusing on real-world myths first and other stuff later vs. never getting around to the other stuff at all is negligable. That said, nobody I know of has said to completely disregard anything that isn\u2019t historical. The closest you get to that is when I said that they should focus on publishing stuff related to real-world mythology, <i>plus</i> a toolkit to empower the players to make up their own stuff if they so choose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35198#post35198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't mean that effort shouldn't be spent on them. Development effort should be spent on what the developers feel are good things for the game; not just what a portion of the fans think is the most important part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>True; and they will anyway, regardless of what fans say. Conversely, fans shouldn\u2019t be shouted down because they\u2019re expressing an opinion about what the developers should do that you happen to disagree with. That leads to an argumentative board that tends to drive fans away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T20:24:58-08:00","id":35336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35197#post35197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When White Wolf pitched Scion, it was ancient mythology awakens in the modern days. That's what got me, and a lot of other people, to play it. That's why we've stuck with it when the system is laughable, the books are terrible and the writing is sub-par. That idea, of classical myth in the modern age, is <b>badass</b>. Is it the <i>only</i> badass thing that exists? No. Can other things be equally badass? Yes. But they are <i>not</i> what Scion was claiming it was about when it was released. That's not what we bought into. Can Scion be <i>expanded</i> to include other ideas? Sure, why not? It just needs to be clear that those things are an <i>alternate take</i> on Scion. You don't sign up for a Werewolf: the Apocalypse game and then get handed a pile of material for the Wild West. That's what Werewolf: the Wild West is for. You don't crack open a copy of Romeo and Juliet to read about the battle between the Capulet and Montague crime families of California. That's when you go watch Romeo+Juliet.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A thousand times this. I sunk over a hundred bucks into the gameline because Scion took what I was passionate about (mythology) and gave it an amazing outlet. I'm not opposed to the National Pantheons/Atlantean Pantheon/Superheroes <i>once the core gameline is out</i>. If the devs find time to make a small companion that won't take money away from developing the core pantheons/rules/titans/purviews/whatever then sure, make something to pay homage to the oddball ideas.<br /> <br /> But as Scion is a small gameline already, don't take up potentially limited space with things that we can just do on the forums. Sure, the same could be said for core pantheons as well, but c'mon, half the fun of Scion is the baggage those gods bring with them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T21:18:31-08:00","id":35357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35144#post35144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had this Argument with Telgar myself Raleel. Just let go and agree to disagree. You're not going to convince Telgar that anything from the era of indoor plumbing is Epic enough for Scion. Might as well be arguing how many angels are dancing on the head of this pin.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are, of course, correct. It's funny, too, because I don't even disagree that it shouldn't be in the core book. It's it's own deal, but I don't think it should be banished forever like some have said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T22:49:07-08:00","id":35391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As you yourself noted, you'd have a problem with a minor Greek god(dess) being on the same level as Zeus, but in Scion canon Persephone has associated Purviews and is therefore on the same level as Zeus and Odin. </div> </div> </div>Persephone is an actor in one of the most well-known myths in the world, she is an important Goddess in the Mystery traditions, she plays an active part in the myths of Adonis, Luece and Minthe, is an observer in the myth of Orpheus and is the Iron Queen of the Underworld. I do not have a problem with her at Legend 12. That said there <i>are</i> a number of deities in the more traditional Pantheons whose status I disagree with, such as Kebauet, Bragi, Idun and Quirinus, almost the entire Keepers of the World.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the problem is that you don't want Uncle Sam to be as powerful as Zeus, then the simple thing is to remove the requirement that you need to be Legend 12 to have associated Purviews so that lesser gods don't all need to have Legend 12 just to have Scions that get associated Purviews. That addresses the much larger issue you've stated. </div> </div> </div>It would not solve all my problems with Uncle Sam, but I would welcome an official system for allowing lesser Gods to have Purviews associated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The game is built around this assumption as being the primary path <b>for the PCs</b>: they'll achieve apotheosis and become gods. </div> </div> </div>That is the point: <b>for the PCs. </b>It is a fundamental conceit of RPGs, whatever form they might take, that the PCs are special. It's why the PCs are the only ones who can kill the dragon. It's why the prophecy always refers to a PC. It's why one PC can mow down armies of mooks. In Scion, it's why PCs can achieve apotheosis in a single lifetime when people like Gilgamesh and Theseus and the Pandavas could not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like you're shifting the goal posts here. Your complaint has never been that Uncle Sam has the specific Purview associations that he does and that they're just attributed poorly, your complaint is that he has them at all because of what rules say he must have done to have them. Since you agree he could have done what it takes to have them, the whole Osiris tangent seems entirely irrelevant. Both of them are written up in the rules based on what the authors felt was appropriate to the mythology around them. </div> </div> </div>I feel like I have been unclear, in which case I apologize. My line of reasoning was this: If you apply the advancement rules for PCs to NPCs like Uncle Sam and Columbia, then you needs must let it apply to all the Gods. Betsy Ross or John Henry, if built like a player was playing them, could definitely earn and spend enough XP to reach a Legend level on par with Vishnu with any Purviews they wish. The problem is, by the same token, why hasn't Osiris picked up Epic Stamina to heal his severed penis? For that matter, why hasn't his wife used her mastery of the Health Purview to grow it back for him? Why hasn't Thor taken the time to learn Water to help in his battles against the Midgard Serpent? Why hasn't Aphrodite not taken the time to learn a single Purview up to Avatar level? Why hasn't Athena bought some Epic Appearance if she's jealous enough of Aphrodite to start a war over it? The list goes on.<br /> <br /> Now, any of those things <i>might</i> have happened in your personal game, but they cannot be a part of the official settings because that would imply that your divine parent doesn't really matter any more because you could argue that in the intervening time the Gods could have learnt any power the player deigns to have associated, because that's what they would do as PCs. Hence they cannot be treated as PCs.<br /> <br /> The only way to avoid a chaotic free-for-all of associations would, therefore, be to stick to the abilities they display in myth or that are attributed to them in religious literature. Osiris does not have Stamina because he does not have it in the myths. Thor does not have Water for the same reason, though if they were played as PCs I do not doubt that both would happen.<br /> <br /> Which leads to my problem with the National Pantheons. There is no myth where Betsy Ross heals the sick, or spreads plague for that matter. There is no myth of Columbia leading the souls of the dead to the underworld, none of John Henry commanding flames. Where are the hymns describing Robin Hood's command over the darkness, or the ones that call on D'artgnan to protect his followers?<br /> <br /> Most of the powers given to the National Pantheons seem to have been given for thematic reasons, not mythic ones. My question is, why should they get this special treatment, when all the other Pantheons need to justify their associations (of course, a lot of the associations in Scion 1e are insane, but that is a discussion for another day)?<br /> <br /> I hope that made it clearer. Again, I apologize for the earlier ambiguity, English is not my first language.<br /> <br /> As a final note, I am not attempting to dictate to the developers what they should or should not do. I am simply putting forth my <b>opinion</b>, that keeping Scion focused on the initial core premise, that of ancient Gods and their modern children battling the Titans, would make for a better product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T23:10:42-08:00","id":35399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35286#post35286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, nobody I know of has said to completely disregard anything that isn\u2019t historical. The closest you get to that is when I said that they should focus on publishing stuff related to real-world mythology, <i>plus</i> a toolkit to empower the players to make up their own stuff if they so choose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to run through this full thread and throw down lots of quotes. But there are at least two people that have said historical stuff only, and plenty of people that clearly don't want it and are compromising with &quot;non-historical pantheons eventually&quot; but often tinged with &quot;eventually meaning in a decade or so, if at all,&quot; and then a few people at least saying, &quot;eventually as in in one of the first non-core-four supplements but not in the core-four.&quot; The whole, &quot;and it can't take away development time/money from the core parts of the game!&quot; thing isn't helping either.<br /> <br /> There's far more people on the thread in the &quot;I don't like the non-historical pantheon&quot; side of things that are expressing their opinion that they don't want to ever see it than people that are expressing the more reasonable middle-ground of, &quot;make a tool kit for it in a supplement.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is kinda funny because that's exactly what most of the &quot;like&quot; sided people seem to want: a supplement/tool-kit for it. Not a complete rearrangement of the game to turn them into a core part of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Conversely, fans shouldn\u2019t be shouted down because they\u2019re expressing an opinion about what the developers should do that you happen to disagree with. That leads to an argumentative board that tends to drive fans away. </div> </div> </div>That goes for both sides of this though.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of people shouting down the opinions that the non-historical and fictional pantheons have a place in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T23:17:53-08:00","id":35405,"title":"","content":"Instead of debate, I happily propose <b>kickstarters</b> for both options so that we can vote with our wallets. If there is enough support for fictional pantheons, then so be it! Even if I do not personally have any interest in such things, I would rather the Scion line stay profitable in the hopes that material I am interested in comes along eventually.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the developers can have a poll to see which non-core supplement the fans would be most interested in seeing next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 12-23-2013, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T08:29:52-08:00","id":35589,"title":"","content":"I don't know if that would be cost effective, aren't Kickstarters hard to make and whatnot?<br /> <br /> I say just cater to me and my preferences exclusively <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T14:18:14-08:00","id":35803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Betsy Ross or John Henry, if built like a player was playing them, could definitely earn and spend enough XP to reach a Legend level on par with Vishnu with any Purviews they wish. </div> </div> </div>And now I'm imagining John Henry going toe to toe with Vishnu. It is an excellent mental image and one I will treasure for the rest of my days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T07:51:24-08:00","id":38731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35144#post35144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But enough of this disgression, anyone know which books JDCarriker (Did I spell that right?) was on in Exalted 2e? I've can't remember seeing him around the Forums. And to keep things vaguely on topic, which books did he write for Scion 1e?</div> </div> </div> </div>For Exalted 2e, he looks to have contributed to the core, Sidereals, Blessed Isle, White and Black Treatises, and Roll of Glorious Divinity II.<br /> For Scion 1e, the Touchstones and Underworlds in Demigod, and co-writing the Tuatha in Companion (mechanics, boons and Titan, primarily).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T11:14:50-08:00","id":49149,"title":"","content":"Seriously, you guys. It feels like every thread on Scion <b>ever</b> ends up talking about the damned WWII and Atlantean pantheons. If I were to go through this thread - which was NOT talking about those topics - and excised those posts, I'd shrink it down to at least 50% of its current size.<br /> <br /> I will say this - Scion has a focus, and that's my primary goal. But I'm sorry, I don't understand the gamer mentality that says a line ought never publish options that they themselves will never use. So no, I'm not making any promises not to revisit some of those concepts in the future. Grouse all you like about &quot;wasted word count&quot; or whatever you like, the fact is I intend to make of this system a broad, useful system for the telling of some great stories about heroes whose power derives from ancient legend, using that power to forge their own myths for the next age.<br /> <br /> I guarantee you that I'll put something in these books you hate. I guarantee that because we're going to put a LOT of stuff in them, over the lifespan of this line, because its potential is broad as well as deep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Regards,<br /> Joseph D. Carriker<br /> -------------------------------------------<br /> \u201cIn Springtime, O Dionysos, To thy holy temple come,<br /> To Elis with thy Graces, Rushing with thy bull-foot, come,<br /> Noble Bull, Noble Bull\u201d<br /> \u2015 Plutarch","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":20}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1242-jdcarriker","name":"JDCarriker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T17:55:59-08:00","id":52012,"title":"","content":"I think this sums up what should be a dev teams response to what seems to be an attitude of &quot;have fun my way or not at all&quot;. I won't get upset by what's in the gameline, if I don't like it I won't use it. I reserve the right to be disappointed if certain things that I think should be included are not. Even in that case, however, the dev team will have put huge amounts of time and effort into their product, and I (and by extension we, the fans) should try to be positive rather than negative. It's very easy to critique decisions in hindsight, and very easy to criticize something from in front of a computer screen that we haven't put heart and soul into. Let's just try to cultivate a better attitude overall, if we can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T22:27:24-08:00","id":52151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JDCarriker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=49149#post49149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I intend to make of this system a broad, useful system for the telling of some great stories about heroes whose power derives from ancient legend, using that power to forge their own myths for the next age.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s definitely a mission statement I can get behind. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T03:14:05-08:00","id":52260,"title":"","content":"I don't mind them existing, certainly not, it benefits me nothing to have them excised.<br /> <br /> I just want them to be covered in splat books that don't contain other real pantheons. Because I don't want to buy WWII or Atlantean and mixing them in with Maori or Gallic or Iberian would really suck for me as those ARE things I want to buy.<br /> <br /> So a book on 'Making your own Pantheon: how to raise your Scions to true Godhood and build a pantheon around the PCs' with options and leeway to fit all sorts of different types of pantheon would rock.<br /> <br /> A book '10 New Pantheons of Europe: Gallic, Iberian, Etruscan, Rus etc.' would be amazing.<br /> <br /> A book '10 New Pantheons That Could Have Been: Atlantean, Axis and Allies, etc.' would be great for those who want them.<br /> <br /> But a book '10 New Pantheons: Iceni, Hunnic, Atlantean, Rus, etc' would upset me.<br /> <br /> Basically mixing them in the same books (except system toolkit style books like a Build your own Pantheon book) is an aesthetic dissonance I don't want.<br /> <br /> Or at the very least place the Atlantean. WWII etc. stuff in a location in the book where I can either start reading after them or stop reading before them. So chapter sequence of Atlantean, WWII, Hunnic, Rus, Gallic OR Hunnic, Rus, Gallic, Atlantean, WWII but not Hunnic, WWII, Rus, Atlenatean, Gallic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 01-18-2014, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T14:57:18-07:00","id":244336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=35099#post35099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're dissembling; none of the scenarios posed could not be accomplished with the original six pantheons' Scions. Which is the point that has been made repeatedly. Not having made-up pantheons costs the game nothing and gains it quite a bite in credibility and acceptance from a plurality of players who are practicing pagans.<br /> <br /> I suppose I should frame it this way: how would you feel if people could just print up bachelor's degrees from your college and have them validated as just as real as yours? Not a perfect analogy, but close enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I'll frame it this way. The Monkey King is a fictional character, made by an author - and we even have his name. Yet, the Monkey King is now a recognized god. Also, in Shinto, a kami is anything which inspires people - and you have shrines all over the place, personal shrines, house shrines, road-side shrines, to a variety of people and creatures. Those are gods. Know who else is a god according to Shinto? Santa Clause. Know who else is? Well, pretty much any fictional character found in a book that people are inspired by - so Sherlock Holmes, Harry Potter, Hello Kitty.<br /> <br /> Uncle Sam is a recognized figure. He inspires people - he is used in US propaganda. Outside the country, Uncle Sam <i>is </i>the USA. So, having him be a god? Totally understandable. Anybody else from folklore? Definitely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T14:41:33-07:00","id":245655,"title":"","content":"The part I don't actually get about the whole WWII gods thing is this; why do they have to be associated with anything?<br /> <br /> Sure, let's say that for what ever reason the gods spread a bunch of Scions around a couple of centuries ago and they led to the WWII pantheons as written. They're young gods who have chosen to branch off and form their own pantheons. That's cool. No problem. But they're young gods. A handful of centuries old at best, for the most part. Why do you have to lower what Legend rating is needed to be associated with a particular attribute or purview? Why can't they simply be young gods still rising into their power? Certainly, some of them may well be struggling to even remain relevant much less define a particular aspect of reality. They are, in effect, the youngsters who have moved out of home and are making it on their own. And that's a pretty damn awesome kind of story to me. I can imagine Britannia sitting down with Athena and going 'I remember when we used to have an empire, mother! I remember when Britain stood for order and shone as a rolemodel to the rest of the world! What happened? And how do I get it back for my people?' and working toward that old world glory, either in the midst of the mainstream Scion war, while also protecting her people from the Titans, or in their own setting.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't mean she's on an equal footing with Athena or any of those other big hitters. She's young and certainly stronger than when she was a 'mere' demigod but not old or powerful enough to claim mastery over an aspect of reality.<br /> <br /> And her children, likewise, would have no favoured attributes to draw on. Not as potent as, say, Thor or Vishnu's kids. That doesn't make their story any less epic or valuable. If anything, the fact that they have to accomplish so much without the 'bonus stuff' the other kids have should make their successes even more epic. In many of their cases (Robin Hood and D'Artagnan to name the obvious two) the little guy with everything against him and with nothing but grit, wit and good friends around him succeeding against impossible odds is the mainstay of their legend.<br /> <br /> Sure, there are some people who will complain and ask 'Who'd want to play someone who didn't get all the cool extra stuff?' but there are others who might appreciate the challenge. And, best of all, you don't have to shoe-horn the system into explaining why they would have a bunch of stuff they probably wouldn't actually have.<br /> <br /> Because if my players are any indication, if you tell people that the WWII gods get to be associated with attributes and purviews at a lower level than written in the book then they're going to want the same thing to apply to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T22:22:41-07:00","id":245884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tashiro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=244336#post244336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, I'll frame it this way. The Monkey King is a fictional character, made by an author - and we even have his name. Yet, the Monkey King is now a recognized god. Also, in Shinto, a kami is anything which inspires people - and you have shrines all over the place, personal shrines, house shrines, road-side shrines, to a variety of people and creatures. Those are gods. Know who else is a god according to Shinto? Santa Clause. Know who else is? Well, pretty much any fictional character found in a book that people are inspired by - so Sherlock Holmes, Harry Potter, Hello Kitty.<br /> <br /> Uncle Sam is a recognized figure. He inspires people - he is used in US propaganda. Outside the country, Uncle Sam <i>is </i>the USA. So, having him be a god? Totally understandable. Anybody else from folklore? Definitely.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, in essence, justifies writing up a supplement for the &quot;new gods&quot; as it were. A bunch of random scions deciding to turn into nationalist symbol-personas makes perfect sense. Yet I agree with the argument presented by Squee that they would not be masters of anything just yet, being very new gods in a largely faithless age. There are no actual temples to Uncle Sam, and Britannia is more of an architectural and design element than a person these days. No one says daily prayers to D'Artagnon or Big Brother and expects some kind of result. <br /> <br /> Holmes, Potter, and Hello Kitty; people do idolize and talk about those characters, and have done so for some time, but that goes back to the original question of: does man make god or god make man?<br /> <br /> The Monkey King got grandfathered in and enjoys several cultural analogs (Hanuman for one), that explains his place among other gods. Assuming that the authoer of Journey to the West wasn't already pulling on some kind of obscure (back then) mythological basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T03:45:33-07:00","id":246063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JDCarriker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=49149#post49149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, you guys. It feels like every thread on Scion <b>ever</b> ends up talking about the damned WWII and Atlantean pantheons. If I were to go through this thread - which was NOT talking about those topics - and excised those posts, I'd shrink it down to at least 50% of its current size.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point... this forum has a lot of contention on that point. One does have to admit that there are supporters of both sides <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T07:24:34-07:00","id":246129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=245884#post245884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet I agree with the argument presented by Squee that they would not be masters of anything just yet, being very new gods in a largely faithless age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disagree a bit here.<br /> Sometimes we can't grasp how people thought, or believed in eras long ago. Or even as recently as 60-70 years ago. It can be difficult to realize that people weren't draft dodgers, that they wanted to fight in WWII, even to the point of faking one's age. (That Capt America movie, the First Avenger? Our hero's attempts at joining the army wasn't some example of hype. It was more an example of what was) People believed in making positive contributions to society, and simply holding down a job was one way. (the memory of the Great Depression was still fresh)<br /> Current western society is too mercenary (&quot;I got mine&quot;) too cynical to believe that earlier decades were somewhat better when it came to having faith in their fellow man, if not in a religious sense. Making contributions to society today is for the wealthy, monied interests, not for an entire population whose very actions were dictated by ideals that once showed the world that we were heroes. <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greatest_Generation\" target=\"_blank\">Greatest Generation</a><br /> Studying the cultural differences of what was then, compared to today is interesting but kinda sad.<br /> But &quot;faithless&quot; isn't a word I would use to describe the &quot;Greatest Generation.&quot; Especially when we see such faith expressed in their very actions, which was far more meaningful than going to temple. I dare say that Uncle Sam had no use for a man on his knees back then.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T18:48:58-07:00","id":246546,"title":"","content":"Nationalism and Faith are two different ideas in this context. I'll give you that the Greatest Generation displayed more patriotism/nationalism than we've seen since their time, but the reality of the world wars did just as much to destroy religious faith as build it (&quot;How can &lt;insert god here&gt; let this kind of destruction happen?!). Not everyone automatically reverts to some kind of religious fervor the instant their lives are in jeopardy, some people's faith will be irrevocably shattered when their whole world view is challenged harshly enough. Granted we're more cynical now, but staring back at the past with starry-eyed idealism isn't doing it any justice either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T20:12:48-07:00","id":246572,"title":"","content":"The idealism doesn't need to be starry eyed, it just needs to be recognized.<br /> <br /> Nationalism is a negative word. There was nothing negative with people wanting to do something for their country in contributing to society in a positive way. But the cynic in me tells me that there is a lot of desire to confuse the patriotism with nationalism. (Back then, &quot;nationalism&quot; was a bad word, since it was seen as Nazism)<br /> <br /> And religious faith after WWII was far better destroyed when adherents were murdered by the millions, most notably by Russia.<br /> <br /> Today we have to really study to understand what was going down in London in 1941. &quot;The Americans are here&quot; was the glad cry that had everyone weeping in relief and joy. And that isn't hyperbole. The UK was on its last legs, and they knew it. They held out in the hope that the &quot;New World&quot; would help save the &quot;Old.&quot; (now if I can find that one writer...)<br /> <br /> Bear in mind I'm not denying some of the negative crap that the US did, but there was a lot of faith being thrown at the country. And for the most part, it was proven out. I understand why some have a difficult time grasping it. It just seems so very unreal by today's fucked up standards that demands that everyone be seen in the same way regardless of the different times, and that everyone should be seen as a glory hounding mercenary that's only in it for the money. We understand that more than we can understand idealism, which is seen today as &quot;na\u00efve.&quot;<br /> <br /> I get the feeling that we're not going to see exactly eye-to-eye here.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T22:28:07-07:00","id":246658,"title":"","content":"People exercise Faith in all sorts of ways, a lot of them secular. Nationalism is just one kind of Faith, from a point of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T05:10:13-07:00","id":246753,"title":"","content":"Nationalism in the context of WWII was seen as Nazism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T11:25:01-07:00","id":246975,"title":"","content":"The thing is, I don't see worship as being necessary. Belief in an ideal, either in a negative or positive fashion, produces an effect. So, those people who are 'against' Uncle Sam provide as much potential as those who are 'for' Uncle Sam. Both acknowledge the idea of the concept of 'Uncle Sam', for example. Actually, I just had this conversation with my sensei, who runs the Shinto shrine just north of Seattle - the Kami of America is enshrined there, recognized as the spirit of the nation itself. So, this means that this kami, which is accepted as the God of America, is worshipped <i>actively </i>right now, in real life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T13:08:44-07:00","id":247088,"title":"","content":"In Scion, worship is unimportant. Gods are not created or empowered by worship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T13:09:35-07:00","id":247089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=246753#post246753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nationalism in the context of WWII was seen as Nazism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't even know how to start addressing all the problems with that sentence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T13:46:00-07:00","id":247105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=247088#post247088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Scion, worship is unimportant. Gods are not created or empowered by worship.</div> </div> </div> </div>To back that up, belief is also irrelevant. No god cares if you believe in him or her. Your belief has no effect on the reality of his/her existence or power. <br /> <br /> Scion's gods are not creations of human cultural zeitgeists manifested as sentient beings They are as real and independent of human belief as rabbits or rocks or roses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T14:09:23-07:00","id":247111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=247105#post247105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To back that up, belief is also irrelevant. No god cares if you believe in him or her. Your belief has no effect on the reality of his/her existence or power.<br /> <br /> Scion's gods are not creations of human cultural zeitgeists manifested as sentient beings They are as real and independent of human belief as rabbits or rocks or roses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, they CAN be altered by contact with human belief as rocks or rabbits or roses can through contact with human industry. So it isn't responsible for their original existence, but it can surely alter them.<br /> <br /> I am not disagreeing with your intended point here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T14:52:36-07:00","id":247136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't even know how to start addressing all the problems with that sentence.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's nice to see how things are today, But it's too late to argue over past beliefs...Einstein; <i>Nationalism is an infantile disease. It is the measles of mankind....&quot;As a citizen of Germany,&quot; he wrote in 1947, &quot;I saw how excessive nationalism can spread like a disease, bringing tragedy to millions.&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T15:35:15-07:00","id":247197,"title":"","content":"There's a fairly big difference between one guy's thoughts on nationalism in WWII era Germany, and WWII era attitudes on nationalism in general. Critics and proponents of nationalism in the WWII era were, by no means, limited to just thinking about Germany and the Nazis.<br /> <br /> Yes, it is too late to argue over past beliefs. People in the past didn't have the beliefs you stated in the post Telgar responded to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T15:56:25-07:00","id":247214,"title":"","content":"What evidence would be convincing? The propaganda that was being thrown around? Quite frankly it doesn't matter now. You will believe what you want. As they did then. Einstein believed what everyone else did. Considering him as a source that lived in those times, if you won't be swayed by people living then, then I'm certain you won't be convinced by anyone or anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T16:21:54-07:00","id":247233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=247214#post247214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What evidence would be convincing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To start, more than one person's views.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T16:53:35-07:00","id":247255,"title":"","content":"No, that sort of thing doesn't convince anyone that already believes differently. Especially those that hold to a 21st century point of view. I can't use Wikipedia to point out Nazi Germany as a &quot;nationalist regime,' because it's Wikipedia. I can't use the propaganda floating around WWII because of what it is. You think a national poll might work? Maybe if it existed. How about a scientist that lived in Germany and fled...o wait...you've already derided Einstein. That's fine. <a href=\"http://www.maebrussell.com/Articles%20and%20Notes/Rise%20and%20Fall%20of%20the%20Third%20Reich.html\" target=\"_blank\">Nazi Germany did the same</a>; <i>To Professor Ludwig Bieberback, of the University of Berlin, Einstein was &quot;an alien mountebank.&quot; Even to Professor Lenard, &quot;the Jew conspicuously lacks understanding for the truth . . . being in this respect in contrast to the Aryan research scientist with his careful and serious will to truth . . . Jewish physics is thus a phantom and a phenomenon of degeneration of fundamental German Physics.&quot;</i>...so you're on the same page as they were....O that page is from William Shirer's opus, &quot;The Rise and Fall of the Third Reich...&quot; But if a physicist that lived there and then won't convince, then I'm sure Shirer's words can be safely ignored...This has pretty much devolved way off-topic. But it does reaffirm my assertion that people can't grasp earlier eras and how they really thought and believed. Must be why the country is making the same damn mistakes....ok. I'm done now. /rant","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T17:36:40-07:00","id":247293,"title":"","content":"1. No one is deriding Einstein, merely stating that his views might not be representative of a large segment of the population.<br /> <br /> 2. No one said Nazi Germany wasn't nationalistic, merely that Germany wasn't the only example of nationalism or representative of the entire movement/belief system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T20:12:58-07:00","id":247397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=247214#post247214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What evidence would be convincing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there is any, because the evidence is solidly not in your favor. The critics of nationalism in countries besides Nazi Germany and Nazi occupied territories (such as the critics of nationalism in the USSR) indicates quite clearly that in WWII era thinking, nationalism was not considered a uniquely Nazi thing.<br /> <br /> Hell, that's not even what <i>Einstein</i> was saying. Einstein wasn't saying, &quot;Nationalism = Nazis, and Nazis were bad, so nationalism is bad.&quot; He was using the Nazis as an example of what he felt nationalism leads to. He was against nationalism in general.<br /> <br /> The problem is that you have to prove that there wasn't significant thoughts on nationalism besides it being what the Nazis were doing. Which is impossible considering that there was a large amount of anti-nationalism sentiment that came out of WWI and the intervening years. There were prominent voices denouncing nationalism before the Nazis rose to power or WWII started.<br /> <br /> You'd need evidence that would show none of that matters. Wat is the evidence that Einstein is more representative than say... Orwell or Russell when it comes to critiques of nationalism?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Einstein believed what everyone else did. </div> </div> </div>Um. Haven't read much Einstein have you?<br /> <br /> Einstein's personal writings do not generally paint a picture of a person that was representative of the mainstream philosophic thoughts of the time.<br /> <br /> And you're name dropping Einstein. What's our reason to treat him as special on this? Why isn't my grandmother, who also fled Nazi Germany, a source that lived in those times? And she's still alive. So I can actually talk to her about these things. My grandfather, before he passed, had some choice rants about the Mussolini government.<br /> <br /> So yeah. I've talked to people that lived in Europe during the time you're talking about before fleeing the Nazis. Not just cherry picked a quote from a famous person. They convinced me of my position on this just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T22:01:18-07:00","id":247468,"title":"","content":"We're derailing here. Let's focus on Scion, okay? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1976,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","user":"Tashiro","date":".  Clarification. 09-03-2014, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T07:01:36-07:00","id":247808,"title":"","content":"*nods*<br /> The argument wasn't going anywhere...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/