{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T19:27:35-07:00","id":264330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=263176#post263176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not varients on Storyteller; the shared system for Scion and Trinity (and who knows? Maybe more games in the far-off future) are our own system rather than one we've licensed from CCP. It uses d10 dice pools and has dots on the character sheet; you can tell it's <i>us</i>, it's just a bigger departure than, say, Exalted is from cWoD. A bit more different than Storytelling (nWoD's system) is from Storyteller.<br /> <br /> And yes, Trinity and Scion share it, to the extent that the nWoD games all share Storytelling but build different special mechanics into the core stats, dice rolls, and mechanics of the game.<br /> <br /> You should be able to run a crossover Scion and Aberrent game, if you really want to recreate The Avengers witn Thor in it.<br /> <br /> It's that core system - the parts without the specifically &quot;Scion&quot; bits - that we'll show in Open Development as soon as we're ready.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's really cool! I love when systems have compatibility with each other, makes for really cool possibilities when you can cross your different stories and characters together!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T07:55:20-08:00","id":385026,"title":"","content":"Do we have any news on a Realease Date?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1350-majortotoro","name":"MajorTotoro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T14:43:36-08:00","id":385584,"title":"","content":"Nope, not really. The core &quot;Sardonyx&quot; system is hopefully closing in on playtesting, but the Scion books themselves are still a ways off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T09:35:39-08:00","id":386385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=385584#post385584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, not really. The core &quot;Sardonyx&quot; system is hopefully closing in on playtesting, but the Scion books themselves are still a ways off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Real soon, now. We've actually been doing some internal playtesting for a while on the various iterations. Very, very quickly moving on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T01:54:55-08:00","id":387170,"title":"","content":"So, I've not been keeping pace with things. Are you going to do what NWoD did and release a book purely on the system mechanics of the shared system used by Scion and Trinity? Or will I only need to buy the Scion:Origins book to have everything I need to get a game going like Exalted does by combining the rules and the default group players are assumed to use into one book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T08:38:54-08:00","id":387437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=387170#post387170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've not been keeping pace with things. Are you going to do what NWoD did and release a book purely on the system mechanics of the shared system used by Scion and Trinity? Or will I only need to buy the Scion:Origins book to have everything I need to get a game going like Exalted does by combining the rules and the default group players are assumed to use into one book?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Trinity Continuum's doing a corebook with the basic rules and a modern setting, including the default splat for that setting.<br /> <br /> Scion: Origins is going to have the basic rules and the mortal-level stuff, allowing you to play mortal-level urban fantasy (with various low-level supernaturals as PC options). If you want to play a Scion, you'll need Hero 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T12:39:49-08:00","id":400698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=386385#post386385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Real soon, now. We've actually been doing some internal playtesting for a while on the various iterations. Very, very quickly moving on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this going to be a iterative process like D&amp;D Next, or will the playtest be pretty much the final system with the goal of finding exploits and errors, not bigger scale design feedback?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T13:54:33-08:00","id":400820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=400698#post400698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this going to be a iterative process like D&amp;D Next, or will the playtest be pretty much the final system with the goal of finding exploits and errors, not bigger scale design feedback?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as far as an iterative process, but we'll absolutely listen to feedback and playtest materials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T19:58:29-08:00","id":402848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=400820#post400820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not as far as an iterative process, but we'll absolutely listen to feedback and playtest materials.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh no doubt! I was just wondering because there seems to be a whole range of these sort of playtests, D&amp;D Next started REALLY rough, while a lot of the Fantasy Flight playtests seem to be almost finished projects, that's not to say they didn't make changes, I'm pretty sure Dark Heresy 2e got some HUGE overhauls after it's playtest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T06:40:07-08:00","id":406641,"title":"","content":"I am thrilled to learn that white wolf's materials have found a home with Onyx Path. However, I'm extremely excited to see Scion 2E is coming as a full property of Onyx Path. When my current pathfinder game ends, I intend to run a Scion game. I always do a couple years prep, so I started digging around for Scion materials. Here I find Scion isn't only finding new life, it's still thriving with so much community involvement. I'm very much looking forward to picking these up as soon as possible. I've already subscribed to the Onyx Path newsletter.<br /> <br /> Origins sounds great from a &quot;base level&quot; introduction to the world. Supernatural (the show) feel too I expect, allowing just enough of that curious, metaphysical, supernatural and oft multi-pantheon exposure. I enjoy the 1E books, so seeing Hero 2E should prove exciting. I look forward to the art as well. The art direction, coupled with great writing, always sets the mood and inspires.<br /> <br /> If there's any relevant kickstarter, which I bet I would have found by now, do let me know. Otherwise, I'll be watching and waiting for any other involvement I may join.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5057-silentinfinity","name":"silentinfinity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5057_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T00:30:17-08:00","id":412500,"title":"","content":"Will Origins and Hero be coming out at the same time?<br /> <br /> As in, at release will I be able to play a Scion or will I be stuck as some kind of epic badass 'mortal' for a few months until the Hero book comes out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T09:15:39-08:00","id":416535,"title":"","content":"I am not in charge of Kickstarter plans, if any, but I believe the current plan is for a simultaneous release of both Origins and Hero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T17:50:41-08:00","id":418144,"title":"","content":"I can't imagine it any other way, honestly. Simply from a &quot;labeling&quot; perspective, releasing a game called &quot;Scion&quot; without the possibility actually playing a Scion in it doesn't sound like a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2219-delta","name":"Delta","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T22:36:58-07:00","id":435313,"title":"","content":"One request from someone who can't pronounce mythological or many fantasy 'names' (made up)... somehow include a way to understand how to pronounce it, I don't know how much room that would take but perhaps a PDF released along the the core-product or sometime after the core-product (2e) is released. Sounds nitpicky BUT... from someone who is challenged in that way, I would appreciate it. If you can't officially do it and can't rationalize it or just don't want to do it.... please, someone from the community consider it. Thanks in Advance. I know it's many, many moons from release but I figure I would request now and see what comes out then it's time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5256-aeternal","name":"Aeternal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T12:25:45-07:00","id":436047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeternal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=435313#post435313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, someone from the community consider it. Thanks in Advance. I know it's many, many moons from release but I figure I would request now and see what comes out then it's time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good afternoon! Since you are asking people from the community, there is a great pronunciation guide created by the incredibly awesome Anne.<br /> (Takes a second to load.)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/pantheons/divine-pronunciation-a\" target=\"_blank\">Divine Pronunciation A</a><br /> <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/pantheons/divine-pronunciation-b\" target=\"_blank\">Divine Pronunciation B</a></b></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T17:15:37-07:00","id":436440,"title":"","content":"Wow! Thanks for the pronouncement guide!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5256-aeternal","name":"Aeternal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T19:24:47-07:00","id":445221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=416535#post416535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not in charge of Kickstarter plans, if any, but I believe the current plan is for a simultaneous release of both Origins and Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Does the shift in this weeks Monday Meeting to &quot;In Development&quot; have any significance for the possibility of the play-test making it into the wilds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T06:06:41-07:00","id":445693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=445221#post445221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the shift in this weeks Monday Meeting to &quot;In Development&quot; have any significance for the possibility of the play-test making it into the wilds?</div> </div> </div> </div>It means we're closer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T09:03:31-07:00","id":458090,"title":"","content":"I'm curious a bit. With the complete dice system having becvome its own production line so to say. Are the books for scion itself currently still developed (except rules stuff that relies on the system) or are they on hold completely until the dice system is finished? (Curious because the later would mean that it will take quite a while after the dice system is finished until the books come out [way longer than with the other variant])","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T06:57:05-07:00","id":458969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=458090#post458090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious a bit. With the complete dice system having becvome its own production line so to say. Are the books for scion itself currently still developed (except rules stuff that relies on the system) or are they on hold completely until the dice system is finished? (Curious because the later would mean that it will take quite a while after the dice system is finished until the books come out [way longer than with the other variant])</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of stuff has been on hold - especially in the many, many places where rules and setting interact - but there's been work done on them. I hope to be able to share stuff with you guys very soon!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T19:54:09-07:00","id":459631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=458969#post458969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of stuff has been on hold - especially in the many, many places where rules and setting interact - but there's been work done on them. I hope to be able to share stuff with you guys very soon!</div> </div> </div> </div>Who is the Scion writing/development team right now? I'm not sure If I know anyone else beyond you. Also are the scion and trinity teams kinda working as one development group until Sardonyx gets off the ground, or are both teams taking that base system and running in whatever direction they want with it independent of the the other team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T22:07:25-07:00","id":459679,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/search?searchJSON={%22author%22%3A&#91;%22JDCarriker%22]%2C%22sort%22%3A{%22relevance%22%3A%22desc%22}%2C%22view%22%3A%22%22%2C%22exclude_type%22%3A&#91;%22vBForum_PrivateMessage%22]}&amp;btnSubmit=&amp;humanverify&#91;input]=&amp;humanverify&#91;hash]=&amp;humanverify&#91;input]=&amp;humanverify&#91;hash]=\">JDCarriker</a> is the developer. Not a frequent poster, unfortunately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T19:46:13-07:00","id":463028,"title":"","content":"Today's monday meeting makes me wonder if the open development of sardonyx will be done through blog posts or if we will get a chance to play around with a simplified draft of the whole system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T07:11:31-07:00","id":463479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=463028#post463028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Today's monday meeting makes me wonder if the open development of sardonyx will be done through blog posts or if we will get a chance to play around with a simplified draft of the whole system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ideally, both. I'd like to put out a playtest document and also discuss certain parts of it over the blog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:08:14-07:00","id":463856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=463479#post463479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideally, both. I'd like to put out a playtest document and also discuss certain parts of it over the blog.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is probably a really good way to go about it, you get the general broad feedback, but you also get focused guided feedback based on the blog posts. That is how Fantasy Flight did it with the Star Wars RPGs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:27:11-07:00","id":463876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=463856#post463856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is probably a really good way to go about it, you get the general broad feedback, but you also get focused guided feedback based on the blog posts. That is how Fantasy Flight did it with the Star Wars RPGs.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts exactly!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T17:39:34-07:00","id":464078,"title":"","content":"I wonder if character gen Heroic Scions will be a little more powerful now. There was a portion of the game arc in 1e right after character gen where you didn't feel that special at all, it didn't last quite all the way to Demi-God, you did eventually get to be pretty cool as a hero, but there was a bit of a overcompensation in the jump up to Demi-God tier play where you suddenly felt more powerful by magnitudes.<br /> <br /> I could see a possibility of shifting some of that &quot;just became a scion/discovering my powers&quot; game space into the mortal book, setting it up so that Heroes start a little more powerful, and in turn are a little bit closer to Demi-Gods in power when they are ready to make that transition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T15:01:02-07:00","id":527073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeternal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=435313#post435313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One request from someone who can't pronounce mythological or many fantasy 'names' (made up)... somehow include a way to understand how to pronounce it, I don't know how much room that would take but perhaps a PDF released along the the core-product or sometime after the core-product (2e) is released. Sounds nitpicky BUT... from someone who is challenged in that way, I would appreciate it. If you can't officially do it and can't rationalize it or just don't want to do it.... please, someone from the community consider it. Thanks in Advance. I know it's many, many moons from release but I figure I would request now and see what comes out then it's time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've made recordings of most of the terms in the Tuatha D\u00e9 Dannan section:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://app.box.com/s/xmq3sn9x8y0641l8k20dig1vl0zzcw0l\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://app.box.com/s/xmq3sn9x8y0641l8k20dig1vl0zzcw0l\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://app.box.com/s/xmq3sn9x8y0641l8k20dig1vl0zzcw0l\" target=\"_blank\"> https://app.box.com/s/xmq3sn9x8y0641l8k20dig1vl0zzcw0l </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't have amazing recording equipment, but I hope it is somewhat helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}